{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade","id":1435985,"title":"On the subject of the Second Inquisition & the masqurade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-19T02:48:05-08:00","id":1435985,"title":"On the subject of the Second Inquisition & the masqurade","content":"A prominent question V5 raises is why does the Second Inquision effectively inforce the masqurade, keeping the truth of kindred society away from the normies? My take on this question is this: The SI is primarily made up of the FBI, the CIA &amp; the NSA, institutions that bolsters themselves on being infallible, efficient and more-than-compitent, and yet the kindred have been able to operate under their noses since their inception. The public have already lost respect and faith in these orginisations, some even go so far as to advocate the abolishment of the FBI. If the public were to learn about kindred society, they would likely lampoon the inteligence comunity for being too incompitent to protect them from this exstitential threat. Thats why I think the SI keeps the secrets, to save face. Alternitivly, the SI might be afraid that if the public were to learn about vamps, and therefore about ghouling and the embrace, undesirable ellement might get their hands on vampire blood and become ghouls or in extreme cases become or create kindred themselves, therefore having enough power to overthrow the goverment. Do Y'all think I'm on the money on this, or do you have an alternative theory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","user":"AscentionTheMage","date":". 02-19-2021, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T03:46:33-08:00","id":1435989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade#post1435985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A prominent question V5 raises is why does the Second Inquision effectively inforce the masqurade, keeping the truth of kindred society away from the normies? My take on this question is this: The SI is primarily made up of the FBI, the CIA &amp; the NSA, institutions that bolsters themselves on being infallible, efficient and more-than-compitent, and yet the kindred have been able to operate under their noses since their inception. The public have already lost respect and faith in these orginisations, some even go so far as to advocate the abolishment of the FBI. If the public were to learn about kindred society, they would likely lampoon the inteligence comunity for being too incompitent to protect them from this exstitential threat. Thats why I think the SI keeps the secrets, to save face. Alternitivly, the SI might be afraid that if the public were to learn about vamps, and therefore about ghouling and the embrace, undesirable ellement might get their hands on vampire blood and become ghouls or in extreme cases become or create kindred themselves, therefore having enough power to overthrow the goverment. Do Y'all think I'm on the money on this, or do you have an alternative theory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with some of your interpretation.<br /> <br /> The government doesn't want to effectively destroy human society. As stated by Matthew Dawkins, information is power and revealing that there's a massive world-spanning conspiracy of living corpse monsters secretly living among you is not going to be like True Blood. It will effectively end life as was previously known. Whatever happens next will be wholly unlike the previous civilization.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like the governments of the setting didn't ALREADY know about the undead. Project: Twilight and the Guide to the Technocracy were both pretty clear that the government is LITTERED with people aware of it but who are usually answering to one faction or another. It's just Pentex, the Technocracy, and various other factions have their own reasons for encouraging agents to keep things under wraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T06:42:55-08:00","id":1436008,"title":"","content":"How much salt do you want to take? <br /> <br /> Saving face is a pretty good explanation. Another potential explanation is that, were vampires revealed, how easy would it be for vampires to spin the wheel with their resources and connections and present themselves as an unjustified object of persecution from religious extremists that had to hide? They'll end up a protected species. The other alternative is... mutual destruction. The nasty thing about war with vampires is that they'll convert their enemies and watch husbands kill wives.... yeesh<br /> <br /> Part of the Paradox about the SI is that the larger and more well connected the organization, the easier it is for vampires to come in and kill them all, incriminate them, attack families, or otherwise pull the plug on their operation. The SI needs to remain small and nobody should know what they're doing. Remember that these big agencies are have a HQ and a public adress and you can just google who runs the whole thing. If the top are in on it, they need some plausible deniability. Now, Agents connecting from one organization to another? That's dangerous. The FBI does what it says on the tin and is generally considered a force for good, but the CIA is a terrorist organization that sells drugs and interferes with foreign elections; If vampires existed IRL, you'd find them there. A vampire hunter in MI5 wouldn't be able to find and trust the vampire hunters in MI6, nevermind other european agencies. The only saving grace is that foreign inter-agency co-operation isn't really needed since vampires don't really move around that much. I presume it's a third party linking them all together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T19:18:39-08:00","id":1436126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade#post1435985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats why I think the SI keeps the secrets, to save face.</div> </div> </div> </div>That matches the tone of the setting; institutions will not save you because they are vain and mediocre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T19:45:13-08:00","id":1436132,"title":"","content":"I agree with the above and also tend to think the Second Inquisition are pawns of a supernatural faction (vampires, Pentex, many others; take your pick) who already have a vested interest in preserving the Masquerade, which makes it doubly secure. <br /> <br /> I've said it in other threads, but the idea of so much cooperation between intelligence agencies is disbelief-shattering for me. The only way to explain them getting along so well is because of behind the scenes supernatural shenanigans. One of my players who's in the military had this take:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think it\u2019s pretty hilarious the idea that they\u2019re trading information across countries. This is the single biggest point of contention in the real, less _darkness_ world. None of the spy bosses want to share anything. The military doesn\u2019t play nice with the spies. The countries don\u2019t play nice with each other. <br /> <br /> Some perspective here, for instance, US ships can\u2019t even do most of our comms with other NATO ships using 10-20 year old systems because we refuse to share our crypto, even when we have better more advanced systems available as well that we could keep to ourselves. The US military intelligence couldn\u2019t share info on the 9/11 terrorists with the civilian side, and even in the years since it\u2019s gotten almost no better. <br /> <br /> Yet I\u2019m supposed to believe that the top secret guys at the top are sharing secrets and intel on their most terrifying new threats (i.e. undead monsters with mind control powers) with each other? When they might be compromised? Hell, even when there isn\u2019t that threat, it\u2019s almost impossible to share info in the real world, much less in the World of Darkness. This is a game of corrupt power, of corruption at the top, of secrecy and greed and hunger for power. International partnerships and sharing information is\u2026 not really in the cards. <br /> <br /> The annihilation of Vienna is particularly laughable to me. You cannot move and organize the number of men and materials needed to wage that kind of massive battle without leaving a hilariously massive paper trail - and trail of bureaucrats and money behind. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T15:04:10-08:00","id":1436456,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a common theory in the UFOlogy community called \u2018Imminent Disclosure\u2019. The idea is that the government(s) know about aliens visiting earth, they have for a while (Roswell is a commonly suggested introduction) and that the reason why they hide the truth is manyfold but a prominent one is that the revelation would cause a cataclysmic panic that would tend society as we know it apart.<br /> <br /> Religiosity wound enter into a new golden age and/or dark age, there would be War of the Worlds hysteria, there would be widespread terror and the chaos that ensued could see economic failure from bank runs or complete losses of faith in the government/militaries power to defend their citizens with populist movements taking the streets and alien collaborators trying to defect.<br /> <br /> The point is - it would be a huge hassle and would destroy the status quo. Those who benefit from that status quo (read: those with power/influence) want to avoid this at all costs.<br /> <br /> The same principle applies to government sanctioned hunting/investigation operations. The revelations of vampires in our midst could trigger similar catastrophes to the ones proposed by UFOlogists. The powerful individuals who hold the reins of groups like Project: Twilight and the FBI Special Affairs Division would like to avoid that - so make whatever deals or power plays you have to in order to maintain society as is without the masquerade keeping the machine going being undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T19:31:52-08:00","id":1436494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436132#post1436132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the above and also tend to think the Second Inquisition are pawns of a supernatural faction (vampires, Pentex, many others; take your pick) who already have a vested interest in preserving the Masquerade, which makes it doubly secure.<br /> <br /> I've said it in other threads, but the idea of so much cooperation between intelligence agencies is disbelief-shattering for me. The only way to explain them getting along so well is because of behind the scenes supernatural shenanigans. One of my players who's in the military had this take:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/UKUSA_Map.svg/1280px-UKUSA_Map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes\" target=\"_blank\"> Five Eyes - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, I have no doubt that if the United States knows about vampires then so does Britain and so does Australia. From there, it will leak and get picked up by other groups.<br /> <br /> Some Watsonian and Doylist thoughts too.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Doylist</b>: There is flat out no point to making the Second Inquisition a pawn to any supernatural faction without essentially dismissing the need for the Second Inquisition period. Either the Second Inquisition shows the dangers of regular humans to vampires or you shouldn't use it. That's my Doylist view on the subject. The whole point is to explain why the Masquerade is necessary and that if humans knew about the undead, the undead would last roughly long enough to be a bug splattering against the windshield of humanity's car. Vampires need to be secret because they cannot live without humanity and its institutions while humans most certainly can. It's not necessarily a popular view but it's one that I think should absolutely be true in-universe and it is a course correction from 2nd Edition onward that vampires have increasingly been portrayed as invulnerable versus vulnerable due to their powers trumping the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I cite Garth Ennis' THE BOYS as a good example, especially the comic. One thing that Ennis liked highlighting is that superpowers are IMPRESSIVE but in the fact of the dedicated military technology and practicality of a modern military--they're fucking useless. At one point, a PMC is hired to kill the equivalent of the X-men and they do it within a couple of hours with almost zero casualties.<br /> <br /> I think the Second Inquisition should have infiltrators and influencers as well as people using it to fight their enemies but it should always be an independent group because the whole point is that vampires CANNOT control humanity that is aware of them. Otherwise, the story loses pretty much all of its resonance.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Watsonian</b>: In simple terms, the Second Inquisition I think the SI is way too big to be controlled. It's also not like they don't have their own defenses. Against an Antediluvian, no, the SI doesn't have a chance unless you're like me and retcon it being the party responsible for the death of Ravnos instead of the Technology. However, against virtually anything else, they are going to be pretty evenly matched--especially in 5th Edition because Numina now can match up to the 1-5 levels of Disciplines.<br /> <br /> You don't need to have every one have Iron Will to simply have 3 or 4 people checking each other's work and if they find out that Jeffrey has been sending e-mails to an unknown e-mail that he's probably been compromised. Even so, I do think that you can have a &quot;free&quot; Second Inquisition that still has technology provided by Pentex and the Technocracy to be the kind of grunts that can strike at the suipernatural without explictly making them servants of either.<br /> <br /> Both the Hunters Hunted, Inquisition, and Project: Twilight books also note that &quot;human&quot; means Psychic Powers, Faith, &quot;Weird&quot; Technology, and Hedge Magic as ways to fight vampires. You don't need all of them to have it as just having the guy do the ritual that cleanses mind-control after a few days will do it. They don't need to be PERFECT, they just need to be able to fight.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Mix</b>: The Second Inquisition also isn't meant to be the End of Vampire-dom yet. It's a lowering of Defcon, though, and the majority of vampires will NOT team up against the SI when they can throw their fellows under the bus. It also is harder to fight them when the Camarilla has lost so many Elders and is in the state of a civil war. If a vampire gets jumped by a Hunter Team while awake, he has a fairly good chance of murdering them all and escaping. However, a vampire that has their identity blown and is caught in their lair--be they Elder or not--has a very good chance of being killed.<br /> <br /> Its a hard needle to thread that the Inquisition must be terrifying but fightable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T03:40:59-08:00","id":1436531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436494#post1436494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <b>Doylist</b>: There is flat out no point to making the Second Inquisition a pawn to any supernatural faction without essentially dismissing the need for the Second Inquisition period. Either the Second Inquisition shows the dangers of regular humans to vampires or you shouldn't use it. .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's eh... missing the entire beautiful point of vampire. <br /> IE humans are shitty and we'd never rise up against the evil parasites due to either ignorance, greed or cowardice or some combination thereof, and if we were to go against them it'd be out of greed.... Half the joke of the 'Masquerade' is that vampires overkill its preservation for political reasons. Humans are cattle, and hunters were always meant to be little more than a dangerous joke. It's &quot;the world of Darkness&quot; because humans suck, not because of any particular monster (Demiurge excluded). <br /> And from a Watsonian point of view... there's no conceivable way for the SI to possibly be a purely mundane-mortal driven program. It'd be like herding cats only the cats are paranoid and want to murder eachother and have been given guns that they can somehow use... <br /> <br /> The Doyelist explanation'd really be more... the writers were unhappy with the state of vampire and wanted to shake things up? Boom goes the Pyramid. Boom goes the Camarilla as we know it. Boom the Anarchs are big now; The SI are a driving factor for a third of the new story contrivances in v5. Another suspected Doylist reason is, well, 'equality' seems to be pretty important in nuVampire; Blood potency utterly retards the previously powerful low-gens with horrendous side effects, thin bloods get their own unique magic, and humans apparently have their act together.While before it was very clear that low gens&gt; high gens&gt; thin bloods&gt; ghouls&gt; humans, now it's a matter of trade-offs; everyone is designed to be equal, and the SI kicking off is apart of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T05:08:56-08:00","id":1436534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436531#post1436531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's eh... missing the entire beautiful point of vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The subtitle is &quot;Masquerade&quot; and it's not an argument that there's any reason they hide other than fear. The book opens by saying the First Inquisition scared vampires straight. Whether you think they should or not, that's the premise of the game. Your interpretation is fine for your game but its a bedrock of canon that if the Masquerade is broken, humans will destroy vampirekind and we even have an Alternate Future/History where the Masquerade falls and mankind slaughters the undead described in <i>Gehenna</i>.<br /> <br /> It's like my desire to make the Anarchs into the protagonists who everyone should rally behind. No, they're assholes too in canon no matter how much I'd like to say otherwise.<br /> <br /> That's all I'm Super-Saiyin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-22-2021, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T08:19:11-08:00","id":1436548,"title":"","content":"Gonna agree with Phipps here; humans have never been a joke in VtM, even before V5. Yeah, they\u2019re extremely disadvantaged against a Methuselah, but just how many Methuselahs do you have running around in your campaign?<br /> <br /> For that matter, how many 6th-7th Gens are there really in your campaign city? Most are 8th Gen or higher.<br /> <br /> How many have enough Fortitude to soak an incendiary round? Enough Celerity to dodge half a dozen guys with ARs with magazines of incendiary rounds? Enough humanity to even wake up when they hit in a raid just after dawn? How many ghouls does a vamp have that are well-trained and have enough disciplines to be anything but a speed bump to a six-man spec ops squad hitting in that post dawn raid?<br /> <br /> Because pre-V5, those elders who, per the lore, tend to hover around humanity 4 so their daylight dice pools are capped at 4 dice and they have just four rounds before collapsing back into sleep even if they DO wake up... and pouring gasoline all around them isn\u2019t going to be enough to trigger a new check until it\u2019s lit.<br /> <br /> A lot of the \u201cvampires are like gods/mortals are chumps\u201d argument is based around a human versus a vampire at night, not during the daylight hours when the hunters would actually come for them. Sure, 10 dice to dominate or awe vs. willpower 6-7 (pretty typical for special forces types) will overwhelm a target. Doing the same with 4 dice because it\u2019s daylight and the odds of success drop dramatically (not to mention you need to affect half-a-dozen guys at once before they all open fire with their 6 dice Dex+Firearms pool and incendiary rounds vs. your Dex+Athletics capped at 4 dice dodge check).<br /> <br /> Or they just wait out the elder\u2019s four rounds of actions before they collapse back into daysleep and gently carry them outdoors for the sun to do its thing.<br /> <br /> Vampires ARE very powerful creatures, but they also have great vulnerabilities that can be exploited by those even marginally familiar with fictional vampire lore (chiefly, only attack during the day).<br /> <br /> Even an Antediluvian (with Fortitude as one of their clan\u2019s disciplines) can\u2019t stand more than a few rounds of direct sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T08:35:54-08:00","id":1436549,"title":"","content":"The Boys is a pretty terrible comic and Ennis is pretty famous for hating superheroes. Except for Superman, depending on how drunk he is. In the comic the Boys all were hopped up in Compound V to even stand a ghost of chance against supers. The plot armour the boys bore in the comics and the show is rather astounding. In an infantry situation, superpowers would trump human &quot;grit&quot;and &quot;teamwork&quot;. People have known this since the novel Gladiator. That MC fought in WW1 iirc.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T08:49:15-08:00","id":1436551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436549#post1436549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Boys is a pretty terrible comic and Ennis is pretty famous for hating superheroes. Except for Superman, depending on how drunk he is. In the comic the Boys all were hopped up in Compound V to even stand a ghost of chance against supers. The plot armour the boys bore in the comics and the show is rather astounding. In an infantry situation, superpowers would trump human &quot;grit&quot;and &quot;teamwork&quot;. People have known this since the novel Gladiator. That MC fought in WW1 iirc.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think none of that applies to vampires who, in fact if shot with enough bullets, will go down. Also, are completely immobile in the day. Not to mention have animal like panic attacks about fire or getting angry enough.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires are like Batman in Arkham Asylum not Superman.<br /> <br /> Batman is awesome and can defeat an entire army IF HE'S CLEVER AND STEALTHY.<br /> <br /> Running up and attacking the goons with guns will get them killed. Once exposed, he's probably dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T10:11:47-08:00","id":1436557,"title":"","content":"From astonishingly rare to still very uncommon: <br /> -nutjob goverment agents<br /> -religious nutters*<br /> -blood junkies*<br /> -absolute amateurs who're probably running around with garlic, holy water, perhaps a UFO detector. <br /> <br /> *maybe switch these around. <br /> <br /> Overall, never the most inspiring set of protagonists for our vampire villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T13:59:04-08:00","id":1436579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436557#post1436557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From astonishingly rare to still very uncommon:</div> </div> </div> </div>Your contempt is noted. For the record, I'll use V5 lore, but V20 mechanics should they be necessary, just to keep there from being any 'they nerfed vampires to make the SI a threat' arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -nutjob goverment agents </div> </div> </div>Maybe in the 90's; then 9/11 happened and the NSA and U.S. Office of Terrorism and Financial Intelligence (i.e. the forensic accountants) started scouring the globe for anomalous financial activity and then sent in US Special Forces to hit what they thought were terror cells. By 2003-ish they'd figured out the activity was actually the Masquerade and that monsters were running it.<br /> <br /> To quote the books;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Suddenly the old Project Twilight veterans found themselves called in for urgent noontime briefings in sunny Washington courtyards. Their superiors forgave or wiped clean their irregular records, and promoted them to head up nameless units with quiet authority to task and unleash sudden dawn raids.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The American military and black budgets provide these hunters with oceans of untraceable funding, stored in illicit accounts or in tedious-sounding line items.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> We were already drone striking American citizens without warrant or trial in the name of the war on Terror during the Obama years. Do you really think they couldn't do the same to a vampire who's obvious enough to get noticed or just use an Army sniper to head shot them from a mile away with a .50 cal incendiary round? You can't dominate some Air Force pilot looking at you through a thermal camera from the other side of the country and soaking a pair of incendiary TOW missiles (16 dice of aggravated damage each) even with Fortitude is well beyond most vampires.<br /> <br /> And that's just the Americans...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;In addition to the three other ECHELON countries partnered with FIRSTLIGHT and the Newburgh Group, five more nations have provided enough intelligence or muscle to count as \u201csecond-party partners\u201d and get seats at the table during operational planning sessions.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> The Newburgh Group (British equivalent to Project Twilight) gets its own entry. France, Israel, Sweden and Japan and their efforts/involvement are also covered. There's also this...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;That said, it is only a matter of time before such commands emerge on the ground there as well. We specifically expect them in Germany (where the Berlin rising may have already triggered just such a thing), South Korea, Czechia (ESOG Team 4 has deployed into Prague for a \u201ccleansing operation\u201d), Colombia, Jordan, Italy, Uganda, Spain (which has excellent SIGINT capacity for its size), and the Philippines (where President Duterte\u2019s death squads already include random hunter teams).&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, those nutjob government agents are super-rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -religious nutters* </div> </div> </div>You mean the organization brought back under the auspices of the Roman Catholic Church by Pope Benedict XVI and which now enjoys full access to the Vatican's funding and intelligence assets (yes, they have them), not to mention nearly a millennia worth of history dating back to when vampires actually did dare rule openly? The organization that has been cross-training its inquisitors with US Special Forces and has access to all the military toys AND True Faith?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -blood junkies* </div> </div> </div>Not much to say here... they're ghouls so they're a bit superhuman, and if they can last without getting blood bound they clearly know what they're doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -absolute amateurs who're probably running around with garlic, holy water, perhaps a UFO detector. </div> </div> </div>And who also know sunlight and stakes to the heart are things, have known about the &quot;blankbody&quot; effect since it first got used as a plot point on Buffy back in the 90's, and if they ever start working with a priest with true faith, a blessed crucifix and holy water (which can get True Faith 1 by being blessed) WILL actually hurt vampires.<br /> <br /> If they last any length of time they may also end up recruited by one the more professional outfits too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overall, never the most inspiring set of protagonists for our vampire villains. </div> </div> </div>To the contrary, this Roman Catholic finds the Society of St. Leopold VERY appealing, particularly the connection they added to Pope Benedict XVI (whom many of the faithful regard more highly than the current Francis).<br /> <br /> To the point though, if you presume the people in these groups aren't complete morons who immediately rush in on the first vampire they see, but instead surveil and gather intel before striking, mere mortals can be brutally and devastatingly effective against vampires who go and get themselves noticed with Masquerade breaches.<br /> <br /> Consider all the news stories the past five years or so of FBI raids rescuing trafficked women and children all over the country; a hundred rescued here. Thirty-seven just the other day. Multiple simultaneous arrests of perps. In the World of Darkness with the Second Inquisition that sort of cover story would work wonders for explaining why squads of heavily armed FBI Special Affairs Division agents bust down dozens of doors right after dawn to the media because rescuing kids from sex slavery excuses all manner of perceived excess in the execution of warrants (and why you don't get to see any of the rescued kids who are now in protective custody and whose names you'll never learn because their privacy must be protected).<br /> <br /> No, the need for the Masquerade is VERY real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 02-22-2021, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T15:08:30-08:00","id":1436585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436557#post1436557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From astonishingly rare to still very uncommon:<br /> -nutjob goverment agents<br /> -religious nutters*<br /> -blood junkies*<br /> -absolute amateurs who're probably running around with garlic, holy water, perhaps a UFO detector.<br /> <br /> *maybe switch these around.<br /> <br /> Overall, never the most inspiring set of protagonists for our vampire villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they're against a bunch of self-interested sociopathic parasites.<br /> <br /> Also, many of whom are the above themselves. After all, vampires are all blood junkies themselves.<br /> <br /> Besides, being a lunatic religious fanatic who believes in conspiracies is just describing someone who is RIGHT about the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T16:43:46-08:00","id":1436594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436585#post1436585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they're against a bunch of self-interested sociopathic parasites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, flawed heroes are more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, many of whom are the above themselves. After all, vampires are all blood junkies themselves. </div> </div> </div>They also try to subvert local governments to their ends and bind it\u2019s agents to them, so their people are government nutjobs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, being a lunatic religious fanatic who believes in conspiracies is just describing someone who is RIGHT about the world. </div> </div> </div>Cults of the Blood Gods also made it acceptable behavior for a non-trivial percentage of vampires.<br /> <br /> I mean, which is really more of a nutter? humans that worship the necessary First Cause of the universe as a benevolent being who wants you to spread love and forgiveness -or- a bunch of vampires worshipping their ancestors as gods who will arise to wash the world in blood?<br /> <br /> Likewise, as stated, if you believe in government and supernatural conspiracies, you\u2019re right if you live in the World of Darkness (in Mage there are even abductions by umbrood in the guise of aliens where the gauntlet is thin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T18:14:10-08:00","id":1436604,"title":"","content":"It is an unfortunate implication that the Deep State is real and is actually Left leaning progressive atheists.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, authoritarian fascists too.<br /> <br /> It makes me think the Far Right in the WoD has to be all Pentex and the Camarilla.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T19:26:26-08:00","id":1436617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436604#post1436604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an unfortunate implication that the Deep State is real and is actually Left leaning progressive atheists.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, authoritarian fascists too.<br /> <br /> It makes me think the Far Right in the WoD has to be all Pentex and the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually they tried to make the Technocracy the Alt-Right a few years back in that Mage text game that was released alongside the even more cringy We Eat Blood VtM game.<br /> <br /> As I recall it was set in... Sweden I think, somewhere in Europe that was receiving a bunch of Middle Eastern refugees which the Technocracy was trying to stop because apparently non-white people are special or haven't had their Wonder crushed like White Europeans and Westerners have and can damage the local Paradigm they're trying to enforce. The amazing Double-Racism Combo of White People being Spiritually Damaged because of their culture while Non-White People are inherently special and spiritual because of their culture with cherry on top of the Technocracy being very blatantly the Alt-Right, never mind the YEARS of material to establish that the Technocracy would largely HATE those racist troglodytes.<br /> <br /> It was easily the dumbest way I've seen the Technocracy handled in an official WoD product. And I've read several of the early 1E books where they were treated in some truly bizarre and stupid ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T19:37:43-08:00","id":1436620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436494#post1436494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes#Nine_Eyes</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually asked my military player about Five Eyes about a year ago. This was what he said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Me: </b>How functional really is Five Eyes, and how does that gel with the spies/military so absolutely hating to share intel? <br /> Someone cited them in an OPP thread on the Second Inquisition<br /> &quot;I can buy different agencies cooperating because they already do that&quot; <br /> <br /> <b>Military Player:</b> It's not functional<br /> Almost everything that matters is classified Secret/NF<br /> i.e.<br /> Secret/NO FOREIGN<br /> every now and then I'll see something cross my desk that's SECRET / REL TO, but it's usually crap<br /> Certain info is shared, but anything that could identify sources isn't. Nor anything that is sensitive.<br /> FIVEY is a resource for sharing broad ideas, but it's.... I don't know. A relic.<br /> cold war relic<br /> honestly, US resources are so much greater than everyone else, most of what we share is done to keep the ability to use their countries as operating bases.<br /> for reference, consider that most of the spying Snowden leaked and wikileaks leaked regarding us spying on foreign leaders and such would notionally be five eyes stuff in principle<br /> but in the 90s/00s it really fell off. You saw some reemergence with the war of terror, but not really.<br /> Honestly I don't delve too deeply, but my guess is it is mostly a mechanism to reveal by which you can find a way to transfer specific information other countries request, but they have to know what they're asking for to do that. Probably works to streamline approval process. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T21:44:33-08:00","id":1436634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436604#post1436604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an unfortunate implication that the Deep State is real and is actually Left leaning progressive atheists.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, authoritarian fascists too.<br /> <br /> It makes me think the Far Right in the WoD has to be all Pentex and the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is one of the problems with WoD. The game is centralized around Conspiracy Theories (supernatural ones, economic ones, political ones, cultural ones, etc). And sometimes those in-game conspiracy theories can overlap pretty heavily with real world ones since it's been about 30 years since the game came out. I mean look at Werewolf's 7th Generation a cult of child molesters who worked with vampires to attain political power and extended lifespans. That's uhhh... pretty much Pizzagate.<br /> <br /> Looking at these fictional conspiracy theories and then dropping them onto real-world ones is going to make things really awkward because while the conspiracy theories in WoD are all &quot;fun and games&quot; and exist there for the players to deal with or dismantle, real life conspiracy theories are most often delusional and people can end up hurt or killed because of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T21:58:07-08:00","id":1436639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436617#post1436617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually they tried to make the Technocracy the Alt-Right a few years back in that Mage text game that was released alongside the even more cringy We Eat Blood VtM game.<br /> <br /> As I recall it was set in... Sweden I think, somewhere in Europe that was receiving a bunch of Middle Eastern refugees which the Technocracy was trying to stop because apparently non-white people are special or haven't had their Wonder crushed like White Europeans and Westerners have and can damage the local Paradigm they're trying to enforce. The amazing Double-Racism Combo of White People being Spiritually Damaged because of their culture while Non-White People are inherently special and spiritual because of their culture with cherry on top of the Technocracy being very blatantly the Alt-Right, never mind the YEARS of material to establish that the Technocracy would largely HATE those racist troglodytes.<br /> <br /> It was easily the dumbest way I've seen the Technocracy handled in an official WoD product. And I've read several of the early 1E books where they were treated in some truly bizarre and stupid ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, recent years HAVE kind of soured me on the Technocracy. If the secret masters of the Earth's governments really WERE a progressive pro-science group, totalitarian or not, then the world would be a very different place indeed.<br /> <br /> The secret masters of the Earth, whoever they be, DO NOT CARE in this universe and would not care in the WOD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436634#post1436634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the problems with WoD. The game is centralized around Conspiracy Theories (supernatural ones, economic ones, political ones, cultural ones, etc). And sometimes those in-game conspiracy theories can overlap pretty heavily with real world ones since it's been about 30 years since the game came out. I mean look at Werewolf's 7th Generation a cult of child molesters who worked with vampires to attain political power and extended lifespans. That's uhhh... pretty much Pizzagate.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's also Epstein.<br /> <br /> I had a conversation with Lindsay Ellis where she pointed out this very issue and enjoying the X-Files since Fox Mulder is basically no longer a guy to be considered humorous. I pointed out there were no end of conspiracies done by businesses, the government, mass surveillance, and abuses of power. It's just they didn't involve aliens or werewolves.<br /> <br /> A later conversation on reddit pointed out R/Conspiracy used to be &quot;fun&quot; with UFOs but now it was just Trumplandia and anti-vaccineworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-23-2021, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T22:32:56-08:00","id":1436641,"title":"","content":"Bah, I knew this would happen<br /> &quot;Most hunters are lunatics&quot;<br /> &quot;No, Hunters are part of extremeley dangerous....&quot; <br /> <br /> Stop, you just look like you're beating your chest. The society of Leopold, though the model for effective vampire hunters, is still an absolute minority in the catholic system, and also the craziest group the catholics have. The OG inquisition had the full might of the church behind them and acted from a possition equal to the law, these guys still just have a few chapels, and even with increased funding they act from the position of 'terrorist'. The hunters in the FBI are not 'The FBI' with all the might they could have behind them, they're the fringe wackos with rebelious streaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T00:09:58-08:00","id":1436646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436641#post1436641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah, I knew this would happen<br /> &quot;Most hunters are lunatics&quot;<br /> &quot;No, Hunters are part of extremeley dangerous....&quot;<br /> <br /> Stop, you just look like you're beating your chest. The society of Leopold, though the model for effective vampire hunters, is still an absolute minority in the catholic system, and also the craziest group the catholics have. The OG inquisition had the full might of the church behind them and acted from a possition equal to the law, these guys still just have a few chapels, and even with increased funding they act from the position of 'terrorist'. The hunters in the FBI are not 'The FBI' with all the might they could have behind them, they're the fringe wackos with rebelious streaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to point out that you are again ignoring that the central enemy of vampires is....Hunters. Well other vampires then Hunters. Not werewolves, not mages, or demons.<br /> <br /> Hunters.<br /> <br /> Again, the game made it clear that the First Inquisition is what created the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And your argument is kind of weird here because you're saying. &quot;The Society of Leopold is this tiny group and the Special Affairs Division is this other tiny group and none of them are really any real danger to the undead.&quot; Which is kind of a weird disengagement from the material. The whole point of the Second Inquisition is that the Society of Leopold, SAD, and other small groups of vampire hunters have either allied together or joined a larger group that is showering them with recruits and funding.<br /> <br /> Even then, there's also a certain level of SCI FI WRITERS HAVE NO SENSE OF SCALE (see TVtropes.org).<br /> <br /> There's probably 100,000 vampires of every single sect in the world, not counting Kuei-Jin, in the WOD.<br /> <br /> Not even ten thousand for every Clan and the above includes Bloodlines, Caitiff, and maybe Thin Bloods (though their numbers are exploding).<br /> <br /> Prior to the Second Inquisition, there's probably 2000 or so Society of Leopold members, including old priests, researchers, and nuns tending wounds. That's an infintissmal amount to the billion or so Catholics in the world.<br /> <br /> However, 2000 Hunters actually poses a significant fucking threat to those 100K vampires if only for the fact they needed to be able to find them. Now these 2000 Hunters (which if they doubled or tripled in number is now a terrifying number--and that's on the conservative side) with access to all the money, weapons, and information the government has provided. Remember, the difference between the Frog Brothers and the Society of Leopold is the latter actually have training and knowledge of things of what will kill the undead as well as the basic strategy of, &quot;Don't try and kill the undead during the night, stupid. Burn down their haven.&quot;<br /> <br /> If they just killed a total of 1 vampire each (and they may have more but we're balancing hunters like Sullivan Dane who have killed hundreds vs. vampire hunters who die on their first hunt) then that would be 4-6% of all vampires everywhere.<br /> <br /> That is a huge fucking number and a reason for vampires to suddenly go, &quot;Holy shit. What is going on here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe raise the number of missing vampires to 10% with the Beckoning, implosion of the Sabbat, and recent Civil Wars. What the Ancient Romans would call, &quot;Decimation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-23-2021, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T00:35:21-08:00","id":1436651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436646#post1436646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Allow me to point out that you are again ignoring that the central enemy of vampires is....Hunters. Well other vampires then Hunters. Not werewolves, not mages, or demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clear this up: vampires. The central enemy of vampires is vampires. Not hunters or werewolves or demons, vampires. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, the game made it clear that the First Inquisition is what created the Camarilla. </div> </div> </div>It did, and the first inquisition was feasible. The second isn't at face value. Two entirely different animals in entirely different contexts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T01:04:17-08:00","id":1436652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436551#post1436551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think none of that applies to vampires who, in fact if shot with enough bullets, will go down. Also, are completely immobile in the day. Not to mention have animal like panic attacks about fire or getting angry enough.<br /> <br /> Basically, vampires are like Batman in Arkham Asylum not Superman.<br /> <br /> Batman is awesome and can defeat an entire army IF HE'S CLEVER AND STEALTHY.<br /> <br /> Running up and attacking the goons with guns will get them killed. Once exposed, he's probably dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman has a very specific modus operandi. No killing, no guns, he doesnt have potence or fortitude.<br /> <br /> Good points about the daylight issues, but at night then, a group of vampires, with some training in combat, the right equipment and with the right discipline spread, are a nightmare to deal with in infantry situations in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Also i am not a soldier nor do i have any military experience.But neither does Mr. Ennis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T01:45:02-08:00","id":1436656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436652#post1436652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman has a very specific modus operandi. No killing, no guns, he doesnt have potence or fortitude.<br /> <br /> Good points about the daylight issues, but at night then, a group of vampires, with some training in combat, the right equipment and with the right discipline spread, are a nightmare to deal with in infantry situations in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Also i am not a soldier nor do i have any military experience.But neither does Mr. Ennis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh this is true but that's why the Second Inquisition isn't an &quot;I win&quot; button and PCs are able to fight them. They're antagonists but it's not a case where vampires are hopelessly outmatched.<br /> <br /> It's more, and I hate to use this overused metaphor, more like chess.<br /> <br /> The SI made a lot of big bold moves but the Camarilla and Anarchs are in it for the long haul. Plenty of SI successes are because the vampires have OTHER vampires wanting to help them succeed (The Fall of London is in part because Mithras wants to purge its population and the Fall of Venice was because the Harbingers wanted to help) but it's a monster that can't really be controlled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T07:30:43-08:00","id":1436682,"title":"","content":"Honestly, pretending vampires are the biggest enemy of vampires is, to paraphrase MyWifeIsScary, comedically missing the point.<br /> <br /> The biggest enemy of vampires has been the march of progress and, particularly, the surveillance state.<br /> <br /> - Cameras everywhere (virtually everyone can stream video from a device they keep perpetually on their person) that make it harder to hunt unnoticed.<br /> <br /> - The internet and digital records/banking makes it harder to hide your centuries old financal dealings. <br /> <br /> - Newspapers scanning their old editorial into searchable databases make it easier to spot the patterns of predators in humanity\u2019s midst, not to mention who knows when an old photo that would have once been lost in a dusty old archive of you from forty years ago looking just as you do now might surface?<br /> <br /> - facial recognition programs, smart IDs and similar identity theft protection technologies making it harder for you to pass yourself off as someone else.<br /> <br /> - every new tool Big Tech devises to make tracking you easier (so they can sell you things more easily or allow the government to tax you... California wanted cars whose movements could be tracked because they\u2019re getting so fuel efficient that gas taxes aren\u2019t bringing in enough revenue so they wanted to switch to a mileage tax).<br /> <br /> - the COVID shutdowns and procedures seem tailor made to making vampire existence miserable; lockdowns of bars, nightclubs and other social gatherings where hunting is easiest, nighttime curfews keeping people off the streets at night, temperature scans to make sure you don\u2019t have the virus before entering a building, etc. What good are feeding grounds with no one to feed on?<br /> <br /> All of these forces are basically the equivalent of pressures encroaching civilization puts on all predators; forcing them into competition over dwindling safe resources so the weakest members have to into human populated areas to rummage through trash to avoid starvation and end up drawing attention and Animal Control to deal with them.<br /> <br /> Hunters are the vampire equivalent of Animal Control. They generally aren\u2019t targeting elders with secure domains and stable food supplies that don\u2019t draw attention. They\u2019re targeting the fledglings and neonates forced to hunt in ways that draw attention to themselves because all the prime hunting territory is claimed; the ones with maybe a half-dozen dots in disciplines and a decade of experience as a vampire if they\u2019re lucky.<br /> <br /> Elders only get roped in when the hunters notice the patterns of the weaker vampires; the way they avoid certain places where feeding would be easier. If all the bottom feeders you\u2019re tracking stay out of the popular nightclub that\u2019s nearby, odds are good some stronger vampire is using it as their feeding ground and it\u2019s easy enough start surveiling the building using thermal cameras and, once you have a face, using all the normal procedures private investigators have these days to identify and track them without even leaving their office.<br /> <br /> Modern civilization makes it so much harder to escape detection compared to the First Inquisition days that you don\u2019t need the majority support of something like the Catholic Church to put serious dents in the Kindred populations, you just need a comparitve handful of people who aren\u2019t idiots.<br /> <br /> The fact that, once you\u2019ve identified their haven, probably 80% of vampires can be dealt with using a crowbar, a 5 gallon can of gasoline and a match during daylight hours with zero risk is all that really needs be said.<br /> <br /> Sure, there will be vampires that evade the purge when the really professional hunter organizations show up. That\u2019s not the point. The point is unless you\u2019re one of the ones well positioned enough to avoid it (i.e. NOT most PCs) then it\u2019s going to press you to your wits\u2019 end to make it through such a sweep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T07:46:50-08:00","id":1436683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436639#post1436639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, recent years HAVE kind of soured me on the Technocracy. If the secret masters of the Earth's governments really WERE a progressive pro-science group, totalitarian or not, then the world would be a very different place indeed.<br /> <br /> The secret masters of the Earth, whoever they be, DO NOT CARE in this universe and would not care in the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, one of things that's been present with the Technocracy and their efforts since Guide to the Technocracy is that the Masses are the Masses. They try to lead them down better paths only for Man's short-sighted irrationality to drive humanity down worse paths. Technocracy Reloaded starts with a Technocrat admitting that they have failed, that despite all the propaganda they spew, the Union is losing because of the irrationality of Humanity and the Technocracy's own arrogance.<br /> <br /> And honestly given the growth of... well things like anti-vaxxers, flatearthers, the Alt-Right and Qanon, it's not hard to see the Technocracy becoming utterly frustrated at the Masses of today much less how much worse they could be in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Which is actually pretty scary thing given how bad some of those people are in the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T08:34:29-08:00","id":1436686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436682#post1436682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, pretending vampires are the biggest enemy of vampires is, to paraphrase MyWifeIsScary, comedically missing the point.<br /> <br /> The biggest enemy of vampires has been the march of progress and, particularly, the surveillance state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bollocks to that. Fake news, CGI, deepfakes, clickbait, information overload; nobody's believing shit. The biggest threat to rich guys are other rich guys, and the same goes for vampires. Ten years from now, when we've all got convincing CGI software on our minature smartphones, who's going to believe in found-footage of a vampire attack? Also, it's not like we're going one-direction with the surveilance state. There's kickback and resistance and limitations to how much you can do. Unless you're in a few fascist states, you've really not got so much to worry about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - facial recognition programs, smart IDs and similar identity theft protection technologies making it harder for you to pass yourself off as someone else. </div> </div> </div>Now, this one's worth adressing; <br /> <br /> -Identity protection technologies haven't really come that far. Also, when you have money and vitae, it's not too difficult to get someone to fabricate new identities. It might get bad enough that you must do this in advance, but it won't get so bad that you can't do it. <br /> -Facial recognition software can be fooled. <br /> -Thaumaturges can very likely (almost certainly) develop countermeasures to tech based solutions. <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">-Vampires don't really use a lot of the stuff that gets surveyed personally. They don't need to go to the store and they aren't likely to catch a public plane. They can use proxies for near everything like banks and such.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T10:36:35-08:00","id":1436698,"title":"","content":"We'll find out soon what the new Brand Content people think. It was confirmed today on the WoD Discord that Second Inquisition is actively in development now. The first book from Modi's failed run to be confirmed to still be worked on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T10:54:02-08:00","id":1436699,"title":"","content":"Good. At this point there are really two V5 books we need, V5 Sabbat and the Second Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T18:16:12-08:00","id":1436737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436639#post1436639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, recent years HAVE kind of soured me on the Technocracy. If the secret masters of the Earth's governments really WERE a progressive pro-science group, totalitarian or not, then the world would be a very different place indeed.<br /> <br /> The secret masters of the Earth, whoever they be, DO NOT CARE in this universe and would not care in the WOD.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>And for some reason people screamed it made no sense for the Technocracy to be taken over by Nephandi...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T18:18:16-08:00","id":1436738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436737#post1436737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And for some reason people screamed it made no sense for the Technocracy to be taken over by Nephandi...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers of the Throne may not be COMPLEX villains but it is silly to say they're not REALISTIC.<br /> <br /> Ditto, my hate of Pentex has gone down since it turns out the only thing you need to persuade people to pollute the world and kill million is cash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T21:49:05-08:00","id":1436748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436738#post1436738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Seers of the Throne may not be COMPLEX villains but it is silly to say they're not REALISTIC.<br /> <br /> Ditto, my hate of Pentex has gone down since it turns out the only thing you need to persuade people to pollute the world and kill million is cash.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah sometimes I think Pentex and captain planet villains are actually TOO Nuanced That having a goal other than &quot;Make money now ignore six months from now&quot; is all you need. Honestly it makes want to reboot the idea with Vampires of some sort as antithetical to the wyrm since.... they have to fucking live with shit. OR at least exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T23:00:25-08:00","id":1436752,"title":"","content":"^every time the Garou find out about a nefarious wyrm company , it's not due to Gaian spies, its because someone started hedging their bets.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, can you blame me for suspecting the SI? They're no doubt servants for some wallet.<br /> <br /> The first Inquisition was lawfully done by one international organization in an era where communication was slow and the overwhelming majority believed in the supernatural. Many had great faith and could thus avoid significant compromises in internal security. <br /> <br /> The second inquisition is covertly done by supposedly a connected collection of fractions from goverment agencies and a few terrorist groups. Their activities are secretive and very little of the public believes in the supernatural or the work these agencies would be doing cracking down on the supernatural. Whilst this new inquisition has faster communication technologies, those are things that can be used against them. There's virtually no internal security, but also nobody can really know what's internal or not because it's a patchwork organization built up from highly suspicious entities... <br /> <br /> Yeah they're really not comparable. The FI was believable. The SI is bound to be a clusterfuck without a fix.<br /> -The technocracy is controlling everything from behind the scenes, after they finally deemed vampires threatening enough. Not so interesting an answer. <br /> -This is really vampires just culling their numbers and showing how great and necessary the Camarilla is. Which would explain a lot of the plot in V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-24-2021, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T06:26:45-08:00","id":1436792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436686#post1436686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest threat to rich guys are other rich guys...</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's true, why do rich guys try so hard to prevent their workers from unionizing?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf that's true, why do they lobby politicians to support them stamping out our rights?<br /> <br /> Why do they support the police so handsomely?<br /> <br /> Why do they pit us against each other?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy did they stubbornly insist we stay at work during a raging pandemic, risking it mutating into something <i>even worse</i>, instead of letting us get the merest taste of what it's like to not have to bust our balls for them?<br /> <br /> \u200bNo, the biggest threat to rich guys is the poor people they stole from to get rich, <i>and they know it</i>. They're terrified of us realizing that they are cruel, monstrous parasites; they're terrified of us realizing that we'd be healthier without them leeching from us. So that's why there's a Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-24-2021, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T06:42:29-08:00","id":1436794,"title":"","content":"Yet, no revolution. And the thing with the SI is that they're not composed of proletarian comrades, they're -the goverment- and -the church- , two of the biggest sex-partners for the rich and powerful. That's what makes it so absurd. That 'The goverment' (The SI) is after the wealthy elite (vampires) when reality is the two have been holding hands the entire time. The government works for the parasites, not against them. The SI goes against the natural circlejerk-order of things, and it's an inappropriate top-down approach to justice. We don't such have justice in reality, why should we have such justice in game? It's just wishful thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T06:50:38-08:00","id":1436795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436794#post1436794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the thing with the SI is that they're not composed of proletarian comrades...</div> </div> </div> </div>Some <i>are</i>, but you intentionally wrote them off earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T07:58:03-08:00","id":1436805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436795#post1436795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some <i>are</i>, but you intentionally wrote them off earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>The SI, to my knowledge, is big-gov and church. Junkies and amatuers may continue to hunt, but they're not getting absorbed into 'The Man' SI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T08:00:25-08:00","id":1436806,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the problem with the Second Inquisition from vampires is they THINK that it's a massive global conspiracy.<br /> <br /> When it's actually just a dozen vampire hunting organizations given some help by powerful government (and probably corporate) patrons which utterly fucks over vampires who are not nearly as rich or powerful as they think they are.<br /> <br /> You don't need all of humanity to screw over 100K vampires.<br /> <br /> 10K hunters with money, weapons, and politics can shatter their power structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T10:24:44-08:00","id":1436835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436794#post1436794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet, no revolution. And the thing with the SI is that they're not composed of proletarian comrades, they're -the goverment- and -the church- , two of the biggest sex-partners for the rich and powerful. That's what makes it so absurd. That 'The goverment' (The SI) is after the wealthy elite (vampires) when reality is the two have been holding hands the entire time. The government works for the parasites, not against them. The SI goes against the natural circlejerk-order of things, and it's an inappropriate top-down approach to justice. We don't such have justice in reality, why should we have such justice in game? It's just wishful thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nature of history is that those at the top are uninterested in sharing power. They\u2019ll cooperate right up until one of them decides the other has reached the limit of their usefulness and eliminates them.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why the SI makes perfect sense. The human elites at the top have decided that the vampire elite no longer serves their needs and have decided to eliminate them as rivals to the uppermost ranks of power... so they\u2019re killing them and taking their stuff; as the stronger elites have done to the weaker elites throughout history (while the peasants aren\u2019t even considered at all).<br /> <br /> My hunch is the real human powers behind the SI don\u2019t even care about wiping out vampires entirely. They care about taking the wealth and influence of the powerful vampires for their own. Other than as a propaganda tool for the crusade they couldn\u2019t care less about guttersnipe vampires who live in abandoned buildings and only feed off the lower classes. Crime, poverty and hopelessness keep the peasants from organizing against them and having predators who feed on them to keep their focus elsewhere is just one more tool to keep the oppressed oppressed.<br /> <br /> Side-bar: regarding the Technocracy, it\u2019s worth distinguishing the idealist progressive rank and file who see the Technocracy as the ideal tool to realize all the good ends they profess... and their own elites who exploit the rank and file idealists and use them as tools to exert their own fascist vision for reality. <br /> <br /> Compare the rank and file BLM member who wants racial justice and politicians who back them who only care about exploiting racial injustice to line their own pockets instead of moving to actually solve the problem (because if the problem gets solved their jobs are no longer needed).<br /> <br /> The same goes for the Wyrm; ordinary human greed is just its easiest vector for corruption. But there is something spiritually broken in people who already have more money than they could spend in lifetimes still hungering for more and seeking to rob the poor of what little they have to get it (look at who\u2019s buying up all the properties of small mom &amp; pop shops driven out of business by the pandemic while the businesses of the corporate oligarchs were allowed to remain open).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s your angle for Werewolf. The Wyrm isn\u2019t just someone who\u2019s rich because they created something that made the world a better place or by providing top notch service to their customers, treating their employees well and maybe having a nice house and car. It\u2019s the corruption that drives your hedge funds like Mitt Romney\u2019s to short successful companies and drive down their value so they can profit on the way down, gain majority control for a song, then break up and sell off the company\u2019s assets for more profits while putting hundreds and thousands of people out of work.<br /> <br /> Hell, for a modern evolution, Pentex should be the driving force in the green technology movement; replacing genuine environmentalism and respect for nature with the idea that you buy absolution in the form of \u201ccarbon credits\u201d or bogus green tech like wind and solar which burn more fossil fuels to build than they\u2019ll ever produce, require rare earth elements mined using forced labor of indigenous peoples in distant lands, and decimate local wildlife where they\u2019re set up... but it makes you feel good without having to do any real work to make the world better and if that doesn\u2019t feel like the sort of lie the Wyrm would sell I don\u2019t know what is.<br /> <br /> It all fits together once you start following the \u201cmoney.\u201d Under that model it makes perfect sense that Big Government and Big Church would unite to break up Big Blood to further enrich themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T11:12:39-08:00","id":1436844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436835#post1436835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of history is that those at the top are uninterested in sharing power. They\u2019ll cooperate right up until one of them decides the other has reached the limit of their usefulness and eliminates them.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why the SI makes perfect sense. The human elites at the top have decided that the vampire elite no longer serves their needs and have decided to eliminate them as rivals to the uppermost ranks of power... so they\u2019re killing them and taking their stuff; as the stronger elites have done to the weaker elites throughout history (while the peasants aren\u2019t even considered at all).<br /> <br /> My hunch is the real human powers behind the SI don\u2019t even care about wiping out vampires entirely. They care about taking the wealth and influence of the powerful vampires for their own. Other than as a propaganda tool for the crusade they couldn\u2019t care less about guttersnipe vampires who live in abandoned buildings and only feed off the lower classes. Crime, poverty and hopelessness keep the peasants from organizing against them and having predators who feed on them to keep their focus elsewhere is just one more tool to keep the oppressed oppressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>-You're misconstruing the nature of power. Nepotism and cronyism has it's place, and there's the idea that -if X goes down, I'll go down-.. Remember, capitalism for the poor, socialism for the rich. Old money types have no misgivings about bending over to help one of their number that has fallen into financial straits. We don't live in the world of kings and emperors, but businessmen.<br /> <br /> -more notably, the SI is targeting the poorer (relatively speaking) vampires more than the elites, so your argument really falls apart again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T11:25:00-08:00","id":1436849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436844#post1436844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-more notably, the SI is targeting the poorer (relatively speaking) vampires more than the elites, so your argument really falls apart again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, except for:<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat<br /> * The Giovanni<br /> * The entirety of London<br /> * The Tremere<br /> <br /> Which is probably about 70% of the meaningful successes of the Second Inquisition. Yes, other vampires &quot;let&quot; the Second Inquisition hit all of these places but that's because vampires can't bring themselves to unite against a threat when they can direct it to another of their enemies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T11:50:11-08:00","id":1436855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436849#post1436849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, except for:<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat<br /> * The Giovanni<br /> * The entirety of London<br /> * The Tremere<br /> <br /> Which is probably about 70% of the meaningful successes of the Second Inquisition. Yes, other vampires &quot;let&quot; the Second Inquisition hit all of these places but that's because vampires can't bring themselves to unite against a threat when they can direct it to another of their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait? What? <br /> <br /> - Fucked off for war<br /> - Vampire-led Coup<br /> - Not-as-devastating as advertised<br /> - Inside job. <br /> <br /> Hardly a good refutation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T12:08:24-08:00","id":1436857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436855#post1436855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait? What?<br /> <br /> - Fucked off for war<br /> - Vampire-led Coup<br /> - Not-as-devastating as advertised<br /> - Inside job.<br /> <br /> Hardly a good refutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Lost Mexico City and Montreal to the Second Inquisition before the Camairlla moved in.<br /> 2. The Second Inquisition hit the Mauseoleum beforehand<br /> 3. It left London as a burnt out hellhole with either a dead Prince or a dead Methuselah or both<br /> 4. Inside Job or not, the SI killed hundreds of Elders.<br /> <br /> The thing is that if the SI is being helped by vampires that DOESNT MAKE THEM LESS DEADLY.<br /> <br /> It just means that vampires are bone-headedly stupid in their arrogance.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T13:02:44-08:00","id":1436864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436857#post1436857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Lost Mexico City and Montreal to the Second Inquisition before the Camairlla moved in.<br /> 2. The Second Inquisition hit the Mauseoleum beforehand<br /> 3. It left London as a burnt out hellhole with either a dead Prince or a dead Methuselah or both<br /> 4. Inside Job or not, the SI killed hundreds of Elders.<br /> <br /> The thing is that if the SI is being helped by vampires that DOESNT MAKE THEM LESS DEADLY.<br /> <br /> It just means that vampires are bone-headedly stupid in their arrogance.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. While there were certainly opportunistic vampires involved in some of this, like what happened with the Giovanni as they were getting hit by the SI, the Harbingers and their own rebellious Childer at all the same time, that the SI was being brought up alongside the latter two goes to show that it's foolish to discount them.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that part of why the First Inquisition was so successful was that it happened alongside a time of great internal turmoil in Kindred society, the First Anarch Revolt. Many Kindred of power who could potentially reigned in the Inquisition were distracted by the Revolt or actively using them to kill off rivals which in turn would feed the Inquisition, making it stronger. Now in V5 we're seeing a similar era of internal turmoil in Kindred society. We have the Beckoning removing Elders from the field, the Anarchs completely tearing free of the Camarilla, taking the Brujah and Gangrel with them, and alongside all that a new Inquisition has risen, using modern technology to hunt and eliminate Kindred, something that has been getting warned about for <i><b><u>YEARS</u></b></i> within the setting. And of course we have arrogant Kindred thinking they're in control of the situation, manipulating the SI to their own ends. Until they find themselves in the crosshairs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T13:42:05-08:00","id":1436869,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I don't think the Second Inquisition is actually that large and it's not really that new either. The Second Inquisition as shown in THE FALL OF LONDON and THE CAMARILLA books are basically just the same Hunters (HH not HTR) that existed in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> It's the Inquisition, SAD, NSA, Knights of Saint George, Arcanum (who knew those guys would get off their asses), and probably the Lions of Judea. The big difference is this comparatively small group of people are now coordinating in the post-internet and War on Terror Age.<br /> <br /> The big difference is that they now have people who will let them carry explosives and automatic weapons across borders as well as cover up their crimes like vampires can do. The society that protected the undead from &quot;domestic terrorists&quot; and &quot;religious fanatics&quot; no longer does that because they have friends in high places and anonymity.<br /> <br /> They've recruited a lot more people and have a much larger budget but they don't actually have to be a NEW thing to be so much more dangerous. The great destabilizer for Kindred is not that humans have turned on them en masse, it's that there's now a bunch of Hunters who know garlic doesn't work and can prevent the cops from intervening when a number of houses burn down.<br /> <br /> My view of the SI is this:<br /> <br /> <b>Kindred's Perspective</b>: They think of it as the Technocracy or are utterly unconcerned.<br /> <br /> <b>Reality</b>: They're more like three times the size of what they used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T23:11:42-08:00","id":1436943,"title":"","content":"A problem I have with a lot of your explanations is that you're completely relying on the assumption that kindred are uniformly a group of utterly asinine morons. If your plan hinges on the mistakes of your enemy, it's not a great plan. Using Pre-V5 rules, it wouldn't take long for a coterie of neonates to completely unravel the local SI. Again, the more people involved, the larger the budget, the easier it is for vampires to find the SI and crawl in and kill everyone and or/take their families.<br /> <br /> The SI kinda work on the grounds of 'Remember that time the rich vampires got some mortals together to cull everyone with anarch sympathies, and passed it off as some grand mortal conspiracy and a reason to be Camarilla?' which, of course, totally undermines the camarilla once people realise such an obvious ploy. (I suppose they'll mark it as the work of a few radical elders). It doesn't work at all from a 'look how arrogant the vampires are' because vampires generally lean towards paranoia rather than undeserved confidence, and it doesn't work from a 'mortals are scary' standpoint because clearly it was vampires (and their wanton stupidity) all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T02:49:39-08:00","id":1436963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436943#post1436943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem I have with a lot of your explanations is that you're completely relying on the assumption that kindred are uniformly a group of utterly asinine morons. If your plan hinges on the mistakes of your enemy, it's not a great plan. Using Pre-V5 rules, it wouldn't take long for a coterie of neonates to completely unravel the local SI. Again, the more people involved, the larger the budget, the easier it is for vampires to find the SI and crawl in and kill everyone and or/take their families.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious question is, &quot;So how smart do they have to be to have that NOT happen?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or is your foundational position, &quot;Vampires are by nature better than humans at all of this and could never be threatened by an organized group of Hunters even in a time of chaos?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is a thing I DONT ARGUE WITH as a take for your setting. I'm just saying they seem to be going with something different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436943#post1436943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI kinda work on the grounds of 'Remember that time the rich vampires got some mortals together to cull everyone with anarch sympathies, and passed it off as some grand mortal conspiracy and a reason to be Camarilla?' which, of course, totally undermines the camarilla once people realise such an obvious ploy. (I suppose they'll mark it as the work of a few radical elders). It doesn't work at all from a 'look how arrogant the vampires are' because vampires generally lean towards paranoia rather than undeserved confidence, and it doesn't work from a 'mortals are scary' standpoint because clearly it was vampires (and their wanton stupidity) all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, this hot take is one I wouldn't use because the Camarilla behind the Second Inquisition might as well not involve it at all. There's no point to using the SI if they're not the weapon of mortals.<br /> <br /> That's just my view because the only storytelling importance of Hunters should be that they're the result of breaking the Masquerade and showing why Kindred need to be cautious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-25-2021, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T03:05:13-08:00","id":1436965,"title":"","content":"<b>How Night Road handled the SI</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/paint_2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm actually inclined to point to NIGHT ROAD as a pretty good example of the Second Inquisition in use and if you want to avoid spoilers that it is a pretty good storyline to pick up. Basically, the Second Inquisition is something that is sweeping through Arizona and the vampires of the city are divided about how to deal with it. Several prominent Kindred have been killed by it but the primary thing that it has done to them is it has &quot;disrupted&quot; Kindred society rather than actually taken it down.<br /> <br /> One of the funniest scenes of Night Road to me is the fact the Prince doesn't care about the dead vampires it has left in its wake but the fact the Second Inquisition has closed down his clubs and stopped one of his most profitable Blood Trades. He has to shut down numerous ongoing projects and financial dealings to hide them and it's just so goddamn IRRITATING. This actually results in several more deaths among Kindred because fighting over money and resources is the big consequence.<br /> <br /> Its biggest victory is when the Inquisition attacks a blood farm/migrant camp and causes the blood trade to be disrupted (possibly with your help). Vampires are suddenly without their regular blood supply and turn on each other as well as expose themselves. A Methuselah ends up having to be destroyed because it overtly breaks the Masquerade and the PCs must handle it with the Prin ce and Baron's help.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition, itself, makes numerous clumsy, confused, and overt moves during all this that generally blows up in their face. This includes burning down a trailer park where there's numerous vampires living and getting a bunch of innocent people killed, car chases in the middle of downtown, trying to subvert employees of open undead establishments, and their big attempt to kill the Prince and all of his minions at their equivalent of the Succubus Cluib that they let get open.<br /> <br /> The big climax of the story results in the Second Inquisition in Arizona getting slaughtered down to the last man. Basically, because if you've played the game correctly, then you end up being basically Batman in the final confrontation (or just leave the Prince and Baron to rot because fuck those guys--my favorite ending). A 200 year old ghoul hunter for the Society of Leopold is killed and the organization is left in shambles.<br /> <br /> The Inquisition utterly fell apart the moment that they attempted to directly fight the undead and it reminds me of the attack on the Inquisition chapterhouse in Bloodlines. If you can locate them and their base then they're very squishy. However, the Inquisitions disruption of vampire businesses and activities resulted in them fighting it out and numerous vampires being destroyed plus vampires being made vulnerable because they lost their protections.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T03:41:15-08:00","id":1436968,"title":"","content":"-Don't use huge alphabet agencies for your petty city-level grudge; I'd say average intelligence or a little bit of experience as a vampire. <br /> <br /> Vampire society is pretty darwinistic; the idiots die (and mostly tend not to be embraced, but you try tell that to your players). Vampires self-police extensively, and many among them are exceptionaally gifted with mental facilties. There are more geniuses than idiots among vampires, and the idiots that do survive do so by hugging the thigh of someone with brains, they aren't independent actors. The biggest liability among vampires, the thin-bloods (Who're mostly a liability because they get abandoned, not because of any physiological shortcomming) don't really have the connections to other vampires to do damage with big agencies when they do fold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T04:26:42-08:00","id":1436970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436968#post1436968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Don't use huge alphabet agencies for your petty city-level grudge; I'd say average intelligence or a little bit of experience as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Vampire society is pretty darwinistic; the idiots die (and mostly tend not to be embraced, but you try tell that to your players). Vampires self-police extensively, and many among them are exceptionaally gifted with mental facilties. There are more geniuses than idiots among vampires, and the idiots that do survive do so by hugging the thigh of someone with brains, they aren't independent actors. The biggest liability among vampires, the thin-bloods (Who're mostly a liability because they get abandoned, not because of any physiological shortcomming) don't really have the connections to other vampires to do damage with big agencies when they do fold.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I like is the mistreatment of Thin Bloods basically have them respond to the Second Inquisition by telling them everything or trying to join up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T04:31:47-08:00","id":1436972,"title":"","content":"I'd worry about getting disected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T05:56:46-08:00","id":1436982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436972#post1436972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd worry about getting disected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, there's enough for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T09:27:31-08:00","id":1437002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1436943#post1436943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem I have with a lot of your explanations is that you're completely relying on the assumption that kindred are uniformly a group of utterly asinine morons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t have to be uniform and intellect has never stopped people from making dumbass decisions, particularly when stressed and emotions come into play.<br /> <br /> Because that\u2019s the real vulnerability on the behavioral side of vampires. The best adjusted can completely lose control when angry, hungry or scared and three of the Cam\u2019s core clans have additional mental health issues as their clan curses; anger management (Brujah), outright derangement (Malkavian), and whatever you call going into a fugue state when exposed to beauty (Toreador).<br /> <br /> And once you\u2019re aware vampires exist it doesn\u2019t take a genius to hunt them. You don\u2019t have to approach a vampire to watch the crowds entering and exiting a nightclub with a thermal camera, nor to hire a PI to track down a license plate to an address or rummage through the trash for receipts because \u201cyour spouse is having an affair.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now throw in intelligence agency capabilities; access to bank records (why are their no food bills? why are they accessing Swiss accounts that are a hundred years old?), listening devices (including the kind that puts an invisible laser on a window so there\u2019s nothing in the building to find), drones, contact tracing, etc.<br /> <br /> Identify, Investigate, Plan, Act is not exactly rocket science, particularly when you\u2019re not acting alone (which even without the SI angle is how Project Twilight and the Society of St. Leopold typically handle vampires).<br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t mean their invincible on an individual basis, but the SI has more than enough tools to disrupt your average vampire city to the point its existing power structure collapses (and once that happens the power vacuum will draw a bunch of other vamps to make mistakes because their greed gets the better of their common sense).<br /> <br /> Hell, just think what last summer\u2019s riots would have plausibly done to stress out Kindred society. They may not have been the targets, but when city blocks go up in flames that\u2019s bound to make any vampires in the area nervous... and that fear will lead to mistakes that people who know what to look for can exploit.<br /> <br /> In the \u201cnever let a crisis go to waste\u201d school of thought, the SI was probably cleaning up in 2020. They didn\u2019t start the virus or the resulting lockdowns, but those hunting for vampires could certainly see the opportunity that the societal disruption presented because it would force vampires to adapt their hunting patterns and any time you\u2019re doing something new there\u2019s going to be mistakes made.<br /> <br /> All the nightclubs in the city get shut down and where do all the vamps who used them as hunting grounds go now to hunt? They\u2019re almost certainly going to be hitting some other vamp\u2019s territory and that means strife and for hunters with government sanction and resources, opportunities.<br /> <br /> If I were starting a new vampire campaign, I\u2019d have the city in chaos from an undead perspective. Between the virus and the summer riots, the SI rooted out a ton of desperate vampires, the Prince\u2019s authority is hanging by a thread and Anarchs/Sabbat are taking over whole sections of the city due to the vacuum. That doesn\u2019t even require the SI to still be active in the city or even all that successful... particularly if the city was overcrowded with undead to begin with the basic pressures of a tightening food supply might have actually done most of the work for them.<br /> <br /> While I\u2019m sticking with V20 for mechanics, I do find some of the backstory events of V5 interesting enough to start incorporating... though I\u2019m doing so in real time.<br /> <br /> A major plot element had been the arrival of an ambassador from the Assamites arriving in Court, offering assistance as a sign of goodwill as negotiations are ongoing for their joining the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Now the news just hit the Court about the strike on Vienna with the added wrinkle that the Tremere PC just lost the first-degree bond to his sire and control of everyone he\u2019d blood bound himself (because I\u2019m adapting in the changed clan weaknesses in a V20 format where it makes sense) and no one but the PC knows where the Tremere primogen has disappeared to (he left for desperate meetings with surviving members and heads of the other Chantries to figure out what happened and what to do next).<br /> <br /> The PCs have also made an alliance with the local Giovanni so, once the Tremere fallout has almost settled, I\u2019ll probably blindside them with The Family Reunion next.<br /> <br /> The V5 material isn\u2019t as bad as I\u2019d first thought (its mechanics are still hot garbage in my opinion, but that\u2019s it\u2019s own issue)... it\u2019s main problem is that instead of having it happen in the sort of sequence we\u2019d have experienced it if there had been regular releases from 2004 to today, it got dumped on us all at once as historical events.<br /> <br /> Playing them out real time with PCs makes them a lot more sensible and that includes the rise of the Second Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T09:48:48-08:00","id":1437005,"title":"","content":"A simpler rebuttal is no, most vampires aren't insane morons, but only a fraction of them are ubermensch geniuses like Grand Admiral Thrawn or Lex Luthor. There ARE insane morons too with the Sabbat's shovelheads and those lost to the Beast.<br /> <br /> Most fall somewhere in-between.<br /> <br /> Plus the Beckoning is a good time for the Second Inquisition because a lot of the Vandal Savages and Ra's Al Ghul are elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T11:32:21-08:00","id":1437015,"title":"","content":"Yeah and if the Kindred only had to deal with the SI alone, it wouldn't be an issue. But just like with the original Inquisition, they're not dealing with <i>just </i>the hunters. They're in a time of turmoil where the SI is but one of number of growing fires. Honestly I wouldn't be surprised if some, especially among the older Kindred in the Camarilla and Sabbat, only see the SI as an irritant, that it's impossible for mere humans to be a serious threat against them. An attitude that works in the favor of the SI as it means less Kindred resources are being brought to bare against them in the short term, allowing them to gain more experience and knowledge fighting Kindred.<br /> <br /> Hell, I wouldn't be surprised if some elders continue to deny that idea even after Vienna and London, rationalizing it as truly the work of their fellow elder Kindred with the SI merely being either pawns of said vampires or vultures swooping in to pick at the carcass afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T12:25:22-08:00","id":1437026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437005#post1437005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the Beckoning is a good time for the Second Inquisition because a lot of the Vandal Savages and Ra's Al Ghul are elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, since I'm using the lore, but sticking with V20 for mechanics, once the Beckoning hits it'll only affect 7th Gens and lower instead of 9th and lower for my campaign.<br /> <br /> I don't want two-thirds of my PCs and 30 of my 40 NPCs in the city compelled to run off into some undefined indeterminate conflict because of some meta-event tied to the mechanics of an edition change (there's all of three 7th Gen NPCs, but there are a bunch of 8th and 9th Gens)... that'd be a lot of work to throw away just to try and align with V5 canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T13:04:37-08:00","id":1437032,"title":"","content":"The main problem with the inquisition isn't that they should be easy to deal with, but that it's practically impossible for all these agencies and a few terrorist organizations to work together hunting vamps. Ya need to be secretive about that kinda thing. You know what's not secretive? Making connections. Bah. It's times like these that I lament that most of the folk who'd agree with me have given up or gotten banned. for some reason I imagine you all sound like battered housewives when you try to justify the SI.9<br /> <br /> I like hunters. I'm not opposed to hunters or groups of more professional hunters, nor do I insist that good hunting groups must be supernaturally augmented (Though it is fun to bring out the HIT marks now and then) but there's something fundamentally <i>wrong</i> with big goverment waging a covert war against vampires. It just doesn't reflect on the absurdities of reality, and good satirical literature should reflect on the absurdities of reality; Big gov doesn't crack down on parasites, it enables them. Also, SAD works great as rogue underdogs, but bringing lots of different agencies into it and playing a police procedural doesn't have any of that appeal.<br /> <br /> Pro hunter excuses:<br /> <br /> -A bereaved, or at-risk millionaire hires former spies and/or mercenaries to take on the vamps that threaten him. (You know, a lot of former spies turn to the private sector to engage in corporate espionage. It's not so far fetched to hire a KGB expert. This is part of the reason why it's silly to go to the FBI for experts when there's plenty of former FBI laying around) Perhaps they're in-too deep with a settite/Baali cult and need to murder their way out.<br /> -A former ghoul gets together his spy/millitary buddies together to help him get his fix.<br /> -ditto, but it's an occultist who wants ingredients; Skin, muscle, heart, fangs, ash, saliva, blood; all valuable commodities on the magic market. A medical practitioner wanting to make a great discovery may work too. <br /> -The leaders of a criminal gang are seeing lots of unusual embezzlement going on, and suspect supernatural involvment; send in the hunters.<br /> -A desperate Vampire, or perhaps a too-loyal ghoul acting on their own, gets a private sector mercs/spies to lay waste to their enemies. The 'vampire' status doesn't even need to be revealed, just say the dude's weird and has some peculiarities.<br /> -<i>Former </i>agents join together to hunt vampires, due to inability to act within their agency, they can only do so now. Are they avenging a traumatic injustice or doing it out of morbid curiosity? Who knows.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any other -non supernatural- related ideas (Hedge mages aren't supernaturals)? I'm mulling over if this should get it's own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-25-2021, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T14:19:24-08:00","id":1437042,"title":"","content":"The thing is, we don't really know the full ins and outs of the SI. Much of what we know is vague stuff largely presented from the Kindred point of view which isn't an unbiased account of them. Nor does it help that the 'Second Inquisition' term is actually a rather nebulous term that can encompass multiple groups even if they don't work together. At it's core, the SI is actually two groups, the Entity, the secret service of the Vatican which has incorporated the resurgent Society of Leopold into and FIRSTLIGHT which is the joint NSA/CIA program that targets Kindreds and also coordinates activities with other aware personal in other government agencies around the Western world. But while these to groups do share information with each and have at times done joint operations, much of their work is done on their own.<br /> <br /> Further there are other groups that fall under the SI umbrella but largely keep to themselves like the FBI's Special Affairs Division. They may from time to time trade info with FIRSTLIGHT but they ultimately doing their own thing. Same with groups from other countries. FIRSTLIGHT is an American outfit and their field agents all seem come from American agencies. Other countries have their own groups that while they do share information with FIRSTLIGHT are again, doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> However such distinctions are largely unknown to the Kindred. All they see are special agents and hunters in military-grade tactical gear. The Inquisition of Old reborn in the Modern Age. After all, the Second Inquisition isn't what these hunters call themselves for they have dozens of different names for themselves. No, the Second Inquisition is what Kindred call all these 'new' hunters. For them there is no different between a team of Vatican hunters and a team of SOCOM hunters. They're all Second Inquisition in the eyes of the average Kindred.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T14:41:37-08:00","id":1437045,"title":"","content":"Well the thing is that it is NOT one large organized group. It is a umbrella term for a bunch of vampire-hunting organizations and hunters sharing resources and supporting one another. The Kindred don't know this, for the most part, because they don't know anything about the Second Inquisition. That's partially why they haven't been able to crush it and the fact that its successes are being propped up by other Kindred trying to use it.<br /> <br /> OPERATION: ANTIGEN for example is a alliance of the Arcanum, SAS, Knights of Saint George, and London Police Department with the secret support of Mithras' human cultists. It doesn't have any influence outside of the UK but it doesn't NEED to because taking down 50% of the vampires of London is pretty fucking huge numbers-wise in vampiredom by itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T14:52:52-08:00","id":1437046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437042#post1437042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further there are other groups that fall under the SI umbrella but largely keep to themselves like the FBI's Special Affairs Division. They may from time to time trade info with FIRSTLIGHT but they ultimately doing their own thing. Same with groups from other countries. FIRSTLIGHT is an American outfit and their field agents all seem come from American agencies. Other countries have their own groups that while they do share information with FIRSTLIGHT are again, doing their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could almost take away if you read between the lines that its not even that these groups are so much better funded and working together as human technology is just getting really good at piercing the Masquerade as presently constituted and the groups that have always hunted vampires are employing that tech to do it more effectively.<br /> <br /> Sharing covert intel without possibility of being intercepted in the early 90's that meant in person meetings or couriers or international land line phone calls (not nearly as common in the days when land lines were the norm and cell phones rare, expensive and service areas limited... Lord, do I remember the jokes about what Mulder and Scully's cell phone bills must look like in the mid-90s) that it turn made it obvious you were communicating 'something.' These days sharing intel on vamps is a text message hidden by the sheer volume of the millions sent every day all over the world and maybe a few code words just in case someone else doing traffic analysis is looking for obvious keywords like vampire, kindred, blood sucker, etc.).<br /> <br /> It could also be that the Cam are, in some sense, correct in their assessment that a massive cull of the Vampire population is going to be needed and the old ideal ratios of 1:100,000 will need to be adjusted (or gone back to... V5 suggests that 1:3000 to 1:10,000 is more the norm in present day cities) to keep their existence below the radar. They're probably exactly wrong on who needs to survive the cull to keep it below the radar, but regardless, in my own campaign city they'd probably be a lot harder to find in a metro population of 4 million if my 40 NPCs were literally the whole vamp population of Boston (i.e. 1:100,000) instead of just the most noteworthy (with the actual population including Anarchs and the Sabbat scouting packs being a lot closer to V5's 1:10,000 range).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T15:08:48-08:00","id":1437048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437046#post1437046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could almost take away if you read between the lines that its not even that these groups are so much better funded and working together as human technology is just getting really good at piercing the Masquerade as presently constituted and the groups that have always hunted vampires are employing that tech to do it more effectively.<br /> <br /> Sharing covert intel without possibility of being intercepted in the early 90's that meant in person meetings or couriers or international land line phone calls (not nearly as common in the days when land lines were the norm and cell phones rare, expensive and service areas limited... Lord, do I remember the jokes about what Mulder and Scully's cell phone bills must look like in the mid-90s) that it turn made it obvious you were communicating 'something.' These days sharing intel on vamps is a text message hidden by the sheer volume of the millions sent every day all over the world and maybe a few code words just in case someone else doing traffic analysis is looking for obvious keywords like vampire, kindred, blood sucker, etc.).<br /> <br /> It could also be that the Cam are, in some sense, correct in their assessment that a massive cull of the Vampire population is going to be needed and the old ideal ratios of 1:100,000 will need to be adjusted (or gone back to... V5 suggests that 1:3000 to 1:10,000 is more the norm in present day cities) to keep their existence below the radar. They're probably exactly wrong on who needs to survive the cull to keep it below the radar, but regardless, in my own campaign city they'd probably be a lot harder to find in a metro population of 4 million if my 40 NPCs were literally the whole vamp population of Boston (i.e. 1:100,000) instead of just the most noteworthy (with the actual population including Anarchs and the Sabbat scouting packs being a lot closer to V5's 1:10,000 range).</div> </div> </div> </div>Overpopulation was always established as a massive problem in the setting. Also, there's actually the argument that Thin Bloods are the most evolutionarily advantaged to surviving.<br /> <br /> They don't have frenzies, they can be active during the day [even if sunlight immunity is rare], and can live off of non-lethal amounts of blood.<br /> <br /> They also don't register as &quot;blanks&quot; and depending on how people justify racism against them in the setting, it'd be interesting to see how that affects thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-26-2021, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T07:13:17-08:00","id":1437108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437048#post1437048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overpopulation was always established as a massive problem in the setting. Also, there's actually the argument that Thin Bloods are the most evolutionarily advantaged to surviving.<br /> <br /> They don't have frenzies, they can be active during the day [even if sunlight immunity is rare], and can live off of non-lethal amounts of blood.<br /> <br /> They also don't register as &amp;quot;blanks&amp;quot; and depending on how people justify racism against them in the setting, it'd be interesting to see how that affects thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s interesting for me, since I\u2019m still using V20 mechanics, and my campaign is how it interacts with Dhampirs (because there\u2019s a PC who is one); they are universally immune to sunlight, can eat food, breathe and do all the things mortals do without even having a blood dependency since they generate their own. But they DO have some of a vampire\u2019s powers and seem to get dragged into proximity to the shadowy world and since, as stated, I\u2019m starting to introduce V5 plot elements into my campaign (which includes the SI) banging out likely outcomes ahead of time is beneficial.<br /> <br /> Of particular interest for my campaign is how the Society of St. Leopold would regard them. They\u2019re not undead, but have some of their powers. So with the general level of fanaticism they\u2019ve been depicted as having I\u2019m torn between their lumping them in as abominations that also need to be destroyed, but with the niggling thought that the whole \u201cnew life from death\u201d might be seen as some sort of miracle.<br /> <br /> Particularly since the Dhampir PC in question has particular merits that enable them to more easily blend in among the undead (pale aura) and detect and harm the undead (clear-sighted and virulent strike). Throw in a dot of auspex, celerity, potence and presence, plus dhampirs\u2019 innate resilience in V20 and that the Dhampir in question is already engaged in a secret war against the Camarilla in the city (for having ordered the murder of their parents) and is already under the care of a Franciscan priest (with True Faith) and I\u2019m debating whether the fanatics of the Inquisition wouldn\u2019t see a potential case of divine intervention in the Dhampir\u2019s existence and try to recruit them (which is still a problem for the PC; because fanatics; just a different one from the typical \u201cdie, abomination!\u201d problem).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T08:42:51-08:00","id":1437112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437048#post1437048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Overpopulation was always established as a massive problem in the setting. Also, there's actually the argument that Thin Bloods are the most evolutionarily advantaged to surviving.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is may be true prior to V5, where thin-bloods had access to disciplines up to level 3 or 4. In V5 RAW, they don't, so hunting is much more difficult and risky, and their ability to clean up after themselves is virtually limited to what a human can do (IE, you're going to be doing a lot of murders if you're not depopulating animal shelters) They're at a monumental disadvantage. Thin blood alchemy is far from an effective remedy to this problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T08:49:32-08:00","id":1437113,"title":"","content":"I've never considered SI to be an organization, but a group of people who know about the existence of vampires and are trying to deal with them. These people are strewn willy-nilly across the world in varying positions of power and influence. Some of the are cabinet undersecretaries, some are special forces operators, some are captains in the Army, that sort of thing. They wield enough influence to be able to bring some force to bear from time to time, under the guise of the War on Terror, etc. They try to share information with one another as best they can.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, when someone gets busted as a spy for a foreign government, it's actually an SI operative caught for passing intel to an SI colleague. Sometimes, those training accidents are SI people plugging a leak. So, it's not a world-spanning shadow government or even an agency. In my interpretation, most SI don't know more than two or three others. Except maybe those who know the most and I'd have them be someone like a major in the Air Force - too easy to make them a politician. Easier to hide as a mid-level officer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But that's just me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26251-the-philadelphian","name":"The Philadelphian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T10:07:08-08:00","id":1437116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Philadelphian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437113#post1437113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They try to share information with one another as best they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they actually do that tho? How do you discern who's hunting vampires, who's a bystander, and who's a vampire mole, when you're all trying to yourself secret to avoid the vampires coming down on you? This isn't being gay in the 19th century, there's no easy code you've all agreed on over the years. You're hunting some of the most dangerous and influentual individuals on the planet. How on earth do you establish who you should share information with? If it's so easy to find out, why haven't the vamps, their tenfold servants, and the thousandfold legitimate authority found out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T10:22:54-08:00","id":1437121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437116#post1437116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they actually do that tho? How do you discern who's hunting vampires, who's a bystander, and who's a vampire mole, when you're all trying to yourself secret to avoid the vampires coming down on you? This isn't being gay in the 19th century, there's no easy code you've all agreed on over the years. You're hunting some of the most dangerous and influentual individuals on the planet. How on earth do you establish who you should share information with? If it's so easy to find out, why haven't the vamps, their tenfold servants, and the thousandfold legitimate authority found out?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a great moment in LA By Night (The Web Series) where Jasper points out the Nosferatu were arrogant about their ability to outfight the NSA because computers are a new creation (relatively speaking)., As such, humans were entirely capable of being as good at it as vampires were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T10:59:52-08:00","id":1437123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437116#post1437116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't being gay in the 19th century, there's no easy code you've all agreed on over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you're forgetting that the Society of Leopold has actually been hunting vampires for centuries longer than most active vampires have been alive. I'm sure they DO have a code for communicating with each other worked out over the course of their eight centuries of official existence (and an ideal way to do it to, such as under the guise of the confessional booth).<br /> <br /> For that matter, in your world how the heck did any spies ever get any intel out of Germany or the Soviet Union or the United States or Great Britain? How did they know who was a sympathizer or mole to avoid their government intelligence agencies from coming down on them?<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't omniscient and sometimes dead simple codes can conceal plenty... ex. of coded text messages &quot;I saw BB at the club the other night. I should introduce you the next time you're in town.&quot; or &quot;FG was hitting the sauce pretty hard last night. Might want to give him a few days to dry out before you call.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know exactly what I was saying. Anyone I informed of my code could do the same. How are you, the almighty vampire, going to notice either of those texts amidst the millions sent in your city every day, much less that they are requests for a hit team against a vampire I've located and a warning to let the heat die down before continuing any operations in the area respectively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T12:04:48-08:00","id":1437128,"title":"","content":"I'm forgetting nothing; The SoL communicating with the SoL is an internal matter. Are you really suggesting their secret signs are known by and even taught to the FBI and so on? I'm not talking about the SoL communicating with the SoL, that should be pretty obvious. I'm talking about the correct elements of one agency making contact with the correct elements of a completely different agency. With conventional spies, they can hand off their information to non-spy authorities to get approval and the ball rolling. With Vampire hunters, they'll need to hand their information to... eh... who's an entity that we can trust in this game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T12:15:19-08:00","id":1437131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437128#post1437128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm forgetting nothing; The SoL communicating with the SoL is an internal matter. Are you really suggesting their secret signs are known by and even taught to the FBI and so on? I'm not talking about the SoL communicating with the SoL, that should be pretty obvious. I'm talking about the correct elements of one agency making contact with the correct elements of a completely different agency. With conventional spies, they can hand off their information to non-spy authorities to get approval and the ball rolling. With Vampire hunters, they'll need to hand their information to... eh... who's an entity that we can trust in this game?</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is that there are weaknesses and the SI will screw up. I also argue that vampires by and large won't automatically be able to wrap up the entire network because of it but are more likely to protect themselves then use it against their enemies.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the SI is invincible. I believe it's just dangerous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T12:47:11-08:00","id":1437137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437128#post1437128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm forgetting nothing</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, George Washington was able to set up a network of civilian spies against Britain without any sort of official government to pass information through, nor magic, nor high technology (the secret there, as I imagine would be the case with the SI, is that each link in the chain only needs to know two others and that recruiting was only done by the furthest links in the chain from the center of people they had felt out and trusted).<br /> <br /> Clandestine communication has been done throughout history; to pretend that somehow it can NEVER escape the notice of the vampires is just nonsense.<br /> <br /> So some member of the Society of Leopold also serves as a chaplain in a war zone and, because he's a Catholic Priest, hears confessions. Some CIA officer coordinating spec ops against terror targets comes to him for guidance and the priest suggests he contact a friend (and fellow SoL member) stateside because he can help. They meet in a sunny park outside the friend's parish, discuss how fucked up the the world is and exchange phone numbers. The SoL finds a vampire, they shoot a text to the friend, the friend shoots it to the CIA officer, the CIA officer rewrites it into a possible terrorist threat in the report to his boss. This happens a few times and someone in the chain associated with FIRSTLIGHT notices this CIA officer is passing up info related to vampires. They meet said officer and see if they can't act as a link in the chain to the intel sources providing the locations of vampires.<br /> <br /> BOOM! You now have an interagency connection. This doesn't have to happen very often before you have a whole network of links. Sometimes one of the links gets compromised, but this has been going on for decades now. There are probably dozens of separate channels between FIRSTLIGHT and the SoL and between the British and Israeli, and etc. intelligence networks.<br /> <br /> This isn't hard. This sorta thing happens every single day inside the intelligence communities of the world, but it just magically can't happen with vampires? Again... Nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T17:27:44-08:00","id":1437163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437137#post1437137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes one of the links gets compromised, but this has been going on for decades now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the network &quot;has been going for decades&quot; and &quot;sometimes a link get's compromised&quot;, you have decades of compromised links.<br /> <br /> Compromised links don't just fizzle out and die, they usually do their work as efficiently as non-compromised links but also pass the data to people who shouldn't have it. That's why cypher exists in the first place. The problem here it's that we're assuming the very intelligence institutions could be troughly infiltrated, so you can't possibly know that the foreign agent that *has* to understand the message and act isn't a mole<br /> <br /> That being said, I do like CTPhipps idea that the Beckoning migth have trown a hefty monkey wrench on vampire intelligence networks. But, of course, when the vampires get their act together the SI will start having trust problems<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But the enemies aren't just vampires, they're also (perhaps mostly) human. SI it's a terrorist organization, and not just by semantics: They did a drone strike on Viena. Imagine if that had happened in the US. We're not talking about burning a house or killing a few people here ...<br /> <br /> They're tinny cells who don't know about each other. But they're somehow capable of moving the resources of alphabet agencies to perform (and get away with) such *trememdous* acts, all w/o the same agencies (the people that aren't &quot;in the secret&quot;, and most of them aren't if you want to keep the tiny cell narrative) knowing shit.<br /> <br /> The misterious *heads* that &quot;know the whole&quot; yet aren't themselves controling a network of big organizations, opperating instead trough small dispersed proxies that don't know about each other. YET<i> at the same time</i> can move the resources of big organizations trough all of the world to help these proxies w/o most of those *same* organizations suspecting anything is off when these resources get moved...<br /> This is what I think enters in the territory of bizarre reptilian conspiracy theory (not saying this is bad in the WoD - but it goes a bit further than just badass-normal).<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Trump knew?, was this what he menaced to reveal to the public after the elections?, this was before or after he was replaced by a robot? :P</span><br /> <br /> *This* is where I would place a team of Agents greasing the bureaucracy, if I went with &quot;a wizard did it&quot;. Or the works of a powerful Elder (maybe an Elder that lost control over this uncanny meta-organization after getting Beckoned).<br /> <br /> Whatever the case the fabled &quot;air forces major&quot;, or whoever is managing this disaster waiting to happen with such efficiency, deserves the title of &quot;wizard&quot; regardless of having Arete or not.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It's truly a thing of wonder, how far this thread has moved from its original purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-26-2021, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T20:25:34-08:00","id":1437186,"title":"","content":"I suppose the real question is what is the best way to use the SI in your games?<br /> <br /> Boogeyman? Cannon fodder? Looming threat off-screen?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T21:27:23-08:00","id":1437195,"title":"","content":"First, the thing about compromised links is that\u2019s why you try to establish more than one; so you can cross-check intel from multiple sources and if a channel is proved compromised you shut it down. This isn\u2019t even super-secret sources and methods here; this is the sort of stuff that Tom Clancy was able to research from public documents and put into novels.<br /> <br /> Second, a serious question then about the strike on Vienna you call terrorist action; at what point is it not a terrorist action, but government policy?<br /> <br /> President Obama ordered drone strikes on targets all over the world including on US citizens without trial. Outside of the far right, that wasn\u2019t considered terrorist action even though there was plenty of collateral damage in those attacks. So at least by the definitions of the US government and media there IS a level of authority where such actions are generally considered legitimate and not terror strikes.<br /> <br /> But what about when the President of Iran orders an assassination of a foreign target and there\u2019s collateral damage? Terror or legitimate and why or why not?<br /> <br /> How about when the head of the CIA appointed by the President and confirmed by the Senate orders a drone strike on a target because of national security concerns? How about when a subordinate designated by the CIA head orders it?<br /> <br /> Because the SI material released so far (mostly in the V5 Camarilla book) doesn\u2019t indicate these are isolated cells; they mention interagency (and international) cooperation and approved black ops budgets in the billions. The Tremere Chantry in Vienna was hit by a joint SOCOM (United States Special Operations Command) task force... meaning approval for the strike came from at least the level of the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff if not the President of the United States.<br /> <br /> Which is why my question before is important... because to label the strike against Chantry in Vienna terrorism, then you also have to label things like the raid that took out Osama bin Laden (where the US entered a foreign country without permission, stormed the compound and killed a woman and one of bin Laden\u2019s kids in the crossfire) as terrorist actions too. Is that a position you\u2019re comfortable with?<br /> <br /> Because let\u2019s be honest here... vampires may be the protagonists of the game, but they are villain protagonists and theTremere leadership in Vienna was soaked with centuries of innocent blood. They absolutely deserved to be wiped out with as much extreme prejudice as delivered to any terrorist cell.<br /> <br /> How many vampires out there would NOT be considered a serial killer by any reasonable legal standard?<br /> <br /> Are the SI really terrorists for (with at least some level of government sanction) targeting the members of a criminal conspiracy organized to protect a whole group of serial killers from the consequences of their crimes?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a good answer for where the line is and what nuances matter in the decisions. Where the line falls for your campaign is something each GM needs to answer for themselves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I intend to run them as heroic antagonists because the majority of vampires in my campaign city are complete monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T21:36:16-08:00","id":1437197,"title":"","content":"I try to make the Inquisition a bunch of psychopaths and not remotely heroic antagonists. It makes the story more interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T22:59:33-08:00","id":1437204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437137#post1437137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, George Washington was able to set up a network of civilian spies against Britain without any sort of official government to pass information through, nor magic, nor high technology (the secret there, as I imagine would be the case with the SI, is that each link in the chain only needs to know two others and that recruiting was only done by the furthest links in the chain from the center of people they had felt out and trusted).<br /> Clandestine communication has been done throughout history; to pretend that somehow it can NEVER escape the notice of the vampires is just nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Stawmaning here? I didn't say never. I'm talking about the crime of scale. (also Washington's methods would be far too primitive for today, let alone against vamps) <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So some member of the Society of Leopold also serves as a chaplain in a war zone and...<br /> <br /> BOOM! You now have an interagency connection. This doesn't have to happen very often before you have a whole network of links. Sometimes one of the links gets compromised, but this has been going on for decades now. There are probably dozens of separate channels between FIRSTLIGHT and the SoL and between the British and Israeli, and etc. intelligence networks. </div> </div> </div> a ridiculous story. I'm not doubting that spies know how to communicate in code. That's ridiculous. (this works the other way round-the NSA wouldn't get anything from the majority of vampire communications) I'm saying they can't tell good spies from bad in the context of vampires (and organizational oversight if we're assuming the whole agency isn't on board with vampire hunting, which is very likely in most cases)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't hard. This sorta thing happens every single day inside the intelligence communities of the world, but it just magically can't happen with vampires? Again... Nonsense. </div> </div> </div>Because magic happens with vampires. Even with the v5 nerfs, Auspex, Dominate, Presence, Obfuscate, the blood bond... vampires have too much of an easy time turning good spies bad, or making good spies seem bad, and so on. Not only can they make an unwitting, unknowing traitor that can fool those around them, they can even command the guy to go postal at his workplace. Pre-v5 nerfs, the SI agent would be spotted with Auspex, tailed with obfuscate, and destroy their organization with Dominate; they might get a few, but they'd never be a global problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-27-2021, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T01:12:48-08:00","id":1437209,"title":"","content":"Maybe it\u00b4s because I`m not from the US but I do think a lot of the actions described in this thread is terrorism.To be honest,the SI makes me uncomfortable because it seems to buy into the ideas espoused in shows like 24 or Homeland that somehow the american goverment just have to work outside the law,torture people etc. to save people.<br /> Vampires might be evil,but they are also fictional.The London police killing a suspected terrorist for running away from them is something that happened.<br /> I suppose I find vampires to be the lesser evil compared to a lot of goverments if only because of the scale of what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25477-perisa","name":"Perisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T02:41:02-08:00","id":1437215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Perisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437209#post1437209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it\u00b4s because I`m not from the US but I do think a lot of the actions described in this thread is terrorism.To be honest,the SI makes me uncomfortable because it seems to buy into the ideas espoused in shows like 24 or Homeland that somehow the american goverment just have to work outside the law,torture people etc. to save people.<br /> Vampires might be evil,but they are also fictional.The London police killing a suspected terrorist for running away from them is something that happened.<br /> I suppose I find vampires to be the lesser evil compared to a lot of goverments if only because of the scale of what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever I use the SI, I emphasize they're a bunch of pricks.<br /> <br /> The things I include when I include them are:<br /> <br /> * The SI targets the Touchstones, slaves, Herds, and connections of vampires indiscriminately. People find their lives ruined, kidnapped, tortured, and killed for no reason other than &quot;perceived&quot; vampire help.<br /> * The SI performs hideous medical experiments because they want to gain vampiric powers for themselves.<br /> * The SI kills witnesses and people in their way without hesitation. An ATF agent questioning smuggling weapons? Well, he and his family get blown up.<br /> * They do go after Thin Bloods that won't help them kill and I make a point that they are the one type of vampire who genuinely can be (if not always are) harmless.<br /> * Many of the SI seek immortality and personal power from vampires because they envy the power rather than out of a desire to protect humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T03:15:42-08:00","id":1437217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437215#post1437215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whenever I use the SI, I emphasize they're a bunch of pricks.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just... nevermind that you think they'll be stopped, how did they start? That's too evil-stupid to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T06:03:23-08:00","id":1437230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437217#post1437217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just... nevermind that you think they'll be stopped, how did they start? That's too evil-stupid to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused.<br /> <br /> Why would they be moral when they're motivated by bigotry, are a bunch of zealots, and are already part of paranoid half-insane organizations to begin with? It's the World of Darkness after all. You don't stay idealistic doing wetwork and being part of conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The reason they succeed is in large part because they're even more evil than your average Neonate and closer to Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T08:47:17-08:00","id":1437241,"title":"","content":"Some bigots can be really nice or selfless people, so long as you're not an object of their bigotry... but that's a muddy subject I don't tend to get into. Wanting to rid the world of vampires, at least, is a noble goal, and sometimes sacrifices should be made for noble goals; that doesn't mean you should wipe three generations because the mother was a ghoul. The level of malice you've described is just plain counterproductive. Too-stupid-to-exist organizations just shouldn't exist, outside of farcical comedy. WoD is satirical, but it's much more low-key than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T12:01:45-08:00","id":1437260,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking in my own VtM/WtA chronicles, I tend to go with the idea of, &quot;Those who hunt monsters eventually turn into monsters themselves.&quot; Many people who hunt vampires or werewolves start off as a bit starry eyed and naive, but if they survive the large majority of them end up being extremely indifferent to others suffering and are willing to do truly terrible things &quot;for the greater good, desperate times call for desperate measures, etc.&quot; Not that every single last one of them would set an apartment building on fire to kill the vampire hiding inside, but quite a few of them would, and they'd be willing to write off any innocent people who died as unfortunate losses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T14:27:45-08:00","id":1437283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437197#post1437197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I try to make the Inquisition a bunch of psychopaths and not remotely heroic antagonists. It makes the story more interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am literally not wired to run a game without some type of heroes in it... so if my players this go around won\u2019t oblige me at least heroic adjacent PCs, I have to pick someone and it may as well be my fellow Roman Catholics (although a version where the Iron Lady never got power).<br /> <br /> I find it especially appropos since everyone but the dhampir has been cozying up with the Giovanni and a secret Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T14:50:32-08:00","id":1437284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437195#post1437195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, a serious question then about the strike on Vienna you call terrorist action; at what point is it not a terrorist action, but government policy?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the point where people defending the SI was arguing that they're not &quot;the alphabet agencies&quot; themselves (that have a direction, and official existence), but rather a conspiracy *within* those agencies that most people actually doesn't know about<br /> <br /> There were countless comments in this thread about the SI being just the hunters, but with more resources. Them not being the whole alphabet agencies, but a cell within that was helping the hunters. These were posted as an answer to this question: How all the intelligence agencies are cooperating all over the world (over enemy countries, even), when in the real world such cooperation it's either impossible or inneficient?<br /> <br /> You never bothered to argue against those commenters, so I assumed you weren't in complete disagreement. I was wrong. However, in that case I feel that the original problems that were dismissed by such an argument are still vaild<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> In no point my argument was moral. Instead you should reflect on this: The drone strikes on Iran authorized by Obama, among other questionable US international practices, are widely known about. The SI isn't<br /> <br /> Think about that.<br /> <br /> Now, I think attacking a capital of the EU it's not really comparable with attacking Iran. Sadly, justice doesn't exist on this world: The US doesn't get away with it because &quot;US are the good guys&quot;. Nor because US it's so sneaky that no one knows. US get's away with it because the countries it targets are weak and can't do shit about it. I don't think it would be quite as easy if US attacked other superpowers (perhaps that's why US never does that?)<br /> <br /> The problem I have with the SI doesn't have anything to do with morals that have nothing to do with the real world, much less with WoD: My point here it's that SI seems to oscilate between a super secret cell within the alphabet agencies nobody knows about, perfectly keping the masquerade while somehow keeping the authorities in the dark ... AND being a nearly omnipotent organization that englobes the world, and doesn't need to keep the authorities in the dark (because they ARE the authorities)<br /> <br /> In the latter case the miracle it's: That all the authorities in the world are agreeing on something, and keeping it a secret at the same time (if such an organization existed, it would be akin to the NWO <i>by definition</i>. Mage notwithstanding)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-27-2021, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T16:03:59-08:00","id":1437292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437241#post1437241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some bigots can be really nice or selfless people, so long as you're not an object of their bigotry... but that's a muddy subject I don't tend to get into. Wanting to rid the world of vampires, at least, is a noble goal, and sometimes sacrifices should be made for noble goals; that doesn't mean you should wipe three generations because the mother was a ghoul. The level of malice you've described is just plain counterproductive. Too-stupid-to-exist organizations just shouldn't exist, outside of farcical comedy. WoD is satirical, but it's much more low-key than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a glass of half-sewage, half-water, it's still undrinkable. Plenty of Pentex executives are the noble, pleasant, and decent family men they believe themselves to be but kill more people than your average serial killer because they slash safety standards for their chemical plant or dispose it in the groundwater. This isn't even me making a point about the World of Darkness, this describes the executives in my local area who have done this unforgivable thing.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Second Inquisition, the assumption people will do the most efficient and effective thing is almost staggeringly unrealistic. The SI is motivated by ideology and hatred that means that they will routinely choose to do things that are not in the best interests of the greater good or their agenda to serve the cause. Vampire victims are, after all, &quot;defiled&quot; and god forbid that they are willingly fed on as part of the herd or someone who has drank of the blood.<br /> <br /> If your goal is to wipe away the filth of vampirism then you will certainly want to destroy those who have been tainted by it even if they're the victims of it. A :&quot;pure&quot; humanity requires being untouched according to the nonsensical ideology that motivates ideals of said groups. It doesn't have to be ALL members of the Second Inquisition and indeed I imagine quite a few of them would be appalled by such an ideology but that kind of conflict is good for roleplaying. At least in my view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437260#post1437260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking in my own VtM/WtA chronicles, I tend to go with the idea of, &quot;Those who hunt monsters eventually turn into monsters themselves.&quot; Many people who hunt vampires or werewolves start off as a bit starry eyed and naive, but if they survive the large majority of them end up being extremely indifferent to others suffering and are willing to do truly terrible things &quot;for the greater good, desperate times call for desperate measures, etc.&quot; Not that every single last one of them would set an apartment building on fire to kill the vampire hiding inside, but quite a few of them would, and they'd be willing to write off any innocent people who died as unfortunate losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I honestly think this is probably the majority of long-standing vampire hunters and why they're actually effective. If you want to kill an Elder vampire then you torch their entire mansion around them and kill anyone who tries to come out during the day. Is it cowardly and murderous? Oh yes, but it works. If you want to get rid of the Nosferatu warren then the best way to do it is to find the mortals they protect, torture them, and then firebomb the little homeless kingdom they've made. Then again, my view of the Second Inquisition is they're the antagonists not the saviors of humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437283#post1437283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am literally not wired to run a game without some type of heroes in it... so if my players this go around won\u2019t oblige me at least heroic adjacent PCs, I have to pick someone and it may as well be my fellow Roman Catholics (although a version where the Iron Lady never got power).<br /> <br /> I find it especially appropos since everyone but the dhampir has been cozying up with the Giovanni and a secret Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call me old fashioned but the majority of my PCs tend to be vampires who try to suppress their worst instincts. They may be selfish and cruel to their enemies but they're people with a fondness for their herds, at least some mortals, and perhaps a cause or something. They try not to kill and are aware that vampirism comes with a heavy cost (some might say a curse) even if they revel in the power they have been given. As such, they make pretty good foes for the Second Inquisition that leave devastation and horror in their wake just like the undead.<br /> <br /> In my current Tampa, Florida game, the PCs are the protectors of the local Thin Blood population and their families. The Second Inquisition and Camarilla both wanting to exterminate the 40 or so people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-27-2021, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T16:35:45-08:00","id":1437295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437284#post1437284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the point where people defending the SI was arguing that they're not &quot;the alphabet agencies&quot; themselves (that have a direction, and official existence), but rather a conspiracy *within* those agencies that most people actually doesn't know about<br /> <br /> There were countless comments in this thread about the SI being just the hunters, but with more resources. Them not being the whole alphabet agencies, but a cell within that was helping the hunters. These were posted as an answer to this question: How all the intelligence agencies are cooperating all over the world (over enemy countries, even), when in the real world such cooperation it's either impossible or inneficient?<br /> <br /> You never bothered to argue against those commenters, so I assumed you weren't in complete disagreement. I was wrong. However, in that case I feel that the original problems that were dismissed by such an argument are still vaild<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> In no point my argument was moral. Instead you should reflect on this: The drone strikes on Iran authorized by Obama, among other questionable US international practices, are widely known about. The SI isn't<br /> <br /> Think about that.<br /> <br /> Now, I think attacking a capital of the EU it's not really comparable with attacking Iran. Sadly, justice doesn't exist on this world: The US doesn't get away with it because &quot;US are the good guys&quot;. Nor because US it's so sneaky that no one knows. US get's away with it because the countries it targets are weak and can't do shit about it. I don't think it would be quite as easy if US attacked other superpowers (perhaps that's why US never does that?)<br /> <br /> The problem I have with the SI doesn't have anything to do with morals that have nothing to do with the real world, much less with WoD: My point here it's that SI seems to oscilate between a super secret cell within the alphabet agencies nobody knows about, perfectly keping the masquerade while somehow keeping the authorities in the dark ... AND being a nearly omnipotent organization that englobes the world, and doesn't need to keep the authorities in the dark (because they ARE the authorities)<br /> <br /> In the latter case the miracle it's: That all the authorities in the world are agreeing on something, and keeping it a secret at the same time (if such an organization existed, it would be akin to the NWO <i>by definition</i>. Mage notwithstanding)</div> </div> </div> </div>Once more I resort to the Watsonian and Doylist point of view regarding this particular element of the game world.<br /> <br /> 1. The Doylist point of view is, &quot;This is the premise of the game. Do you want to enjoy it or not?&quot; Which sounds like a cop out but is actually not, IMHO. Certainly, the premise of the game is that there's 100K superpowered serial killers around the world. The majority of them only kill when they have to or try not to but there's a decent chunk of these that make up for the others by being flesh-crafting Beast-ridden homicidal maniacs that act like the Kurgan at their best and like Rob Zombie's House of 1000 corpses at their worst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HucERcMMuys\" data-code=\"HucERcMMuys\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HucERcMMuys/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is a horror setting that homages 80s slasher movies, gangster movies, and Hammer horror all at once. Part of the suspension of disbelief that drives the game is the fact that either A:] People with modern technology are ignoring these 100K serial killers or denying their existence. B:] They're in on it. Part of why I actually like the Second Inquisition is that I buy B:] a lot more than A:] and without really saying, &quot;The Technocracy and Camarilla control EVERYTHING!&quot; then the latter means the SI is perhaps large enough and influential enough that it can either oppress or recruit the people who do find enough evidence of the undead. There's a balance between the fact that the SI does have to be influential enough to do all it does and cover up vampire existence as well as their own activities [vampires will do the same for them that they do for vampires] but its not any more believable or less than what was before.<br /> <br /> You either buy into idea that the undead and fighting them is a good chronicle premise or not.<br /> <br /> 2. The Watsonian point of view is that the World of Darkness is corrupt enough that the Second Inquisition doesn't actually add that much in the way of conspiracy. It's already a society where people don't question the lies and official reports because the HORRIBLE TRUTHtm is too terrifying to believe. But even then, the Second Inquisition doesn't have to be taken as that big of a deal in terms of how many ripples it causes in mortal society. Again, while the results of the Second Inquisition are MASSIVE in vampire society (albeit, plenty of Kindred continue to ignore them), they're barely a speed bump in the greater 7 billion humans.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition's biggest operation wasn't Vienna, which was apparently, &quot;Al-Qaeda detonates a bomb in an old castle in Austria and European Special Forces and police respond&quot; but The Fall of London where martial law was declared for a week and the result was a massive backlash by the public. Normally, a Second Inquisition operation will consist of something more akin to, &quot;A bunch of guys in an unmarked van burns down a house and if the police show up, they show badges and say that they were investigating a meth lab that apparently blew. Didn't you get the paperwork?&quot;<br /> <br /> The SI have killed probably 2000 vampires or 2% of the vampire race in my games (and probably x10 in regular humans). A massive amount of undead but a handfull of people in the world. How many have they killed in your world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T19:27:15-08:00","id":1437311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437292#post1437292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me old fashioned but the majority of my PCs tend to be vampires who try to suppress their worst instincts. They may be selfish and cruel to their enemies but they're people with a fondness for their herds, at least some mortals, and perhaps a cause or something. They try not to kill and are aware that vampirism comes with a heavy cost (some might say a curse) even if they revel in the power they have been given. As such, they make pretty good foes for the Second Inquisition that leave devastation and horror in their wake just like the undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroic PCs is what I THOUGHT I was getting. Instead, everyone but the dhampir has lost humanity (one dropping three points already).<br /> <br /> They sold out a groups of thin bloods to simultaneously win favor with the Prince and to take over the bagged blood trade the thinbloods were using the proceeds from to help a band of runaway teens from abusive homes... intended to be sympathetic NPCs the PCs might bond with. Instead they identified the thinbloods and got the teens executed because they were Masquerade breaches.<br /> <br /> They decided to expand the blood bag operation by setting up a false charity blood clinic on the local campus, getting people to volunteer blood for a good cause only to turn around and sell it all at a premium.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also getting mortals hooked on drugs supplied by the Giovanni to increase their herds (blood for your fix).<br /> <br /> The Baali\u2019s, who was originally created to be a major behind the scenes villain, has instead befriended them because they\u2019re basically doing his job of helping sink the city into sin for him.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re keeping this from the dhampir PC (who\u2019s focus has been on trying to locate the vampires who murdered their parents 18 years ago when they got left as an infant on a Church doorstep and work their way into an audience with the power behind the Prince who actually gave the order).<br /> <br /> So, no. My tale needs zero additional villains. It needs some heroes because without some heroes it\u2019s just nihilistic garbage that I\u2019d be better off just excising from my life. Right now getting to play the dhampir\u2019s mentor (a truly faithful and humane Franciscan Brother Minor) is about the only part of the whole exercise that\u2019s bearable.<br /> <br /> So, I think what\u2019s needed are some unironic paladins (high humanity, true faith, don\u2019t believe in collateral damage or acceptable civilian losses) particularly once the dhampir PC finds out what the other PCs have been up to (the player knows, but is mature enough to keep the knowledge separate) and will need some additional allies, because the people who were supposed to be the good guys emded up villains as bad as any of the NPCs I\u2019d created to be villains (the PCs were all built with good humanity... the majority of the PCs just didn\u2019t care particularly about losing it once the temporal rewards started flowing for violating it).<br /> <br /> I especially need to smack the majority of PCs in the face that they\u2019re currently the Bad Guys, not the heroes they think they are (because things will be better once they\u2019re in charge, but you have to break some eggs to get there).<br /> <br /> One of them even has the notion that they\u2019ll be able to earn True Faith soon because they\u2019ve been attending weekly midnight Mass with the Giovanni and look at how holy I\u2019m being. It\u2019s so comically missing the point of real faith that I started searching for some sort of Anti-Faith trait to give them instead (maybe the first dot of Daimonion described as \u201cyour faith allows you to now sense the sins of others\u201d... that seems fitting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 02-27-2021, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T19:54:01-08:00","id":1437315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437311#post1437311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroic PCs is what I THOUGHT I was getting. Instead, everyone but the dhampir has lost humanity (one dropping three points already).</div> </div> </div> </div>True but making the SI the good guys isn't going to make the situation better because presumably the game is about the PCs killing and winning over their antagonists. It seems like it would compound the issue.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T19:58:06-08:00","id":1437316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437295#post1437295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once more I resort to the Watsonian and Doylist point of view regarding this particular element of the game world.<br /> <br /> 1. The Doylist point of view is, &quot;This is the premise of the game. Do you want to enjoy it or not?&quot; Which sounds like a cop out but is actually not, IMHO. Certainly, the premise of the game is that there's 100K superpowered serial killers around the world. The majority of them only kill when they have to or try not to but there's a decent chunk of these that make up for the others by being flesh-crafting Beast-ridden homicidal maniacs that act like the Kurgan at their best and like Rob Zombie's House of 1000 corpses at their worst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HucERcMMuys\" data-code=\"HucERcMMuys\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HucERcMMuys/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This is a horror setting that homages 80s slasher movies, gangster movies, and Hammer horror all at once. Part of the suspension of disbelief that drives the game is the fact that either A:] People with modern technology are ignoring these 100K serial killers or denying their existence. B:] They're in on it. Part of why I actually like the Second Inquisition is that I buy B:] a lot more than A:] and without really saying, &quot;The Technocracy and Camarilla control EVERYTHING!&quot; then the latter means the SI is perhaps large enough and influential enough that it can either oppress or recruit the people who do find enough evidence of the undead. There's a balance between the fact that the SI does have to be influential enough to do all it does and cover up vampire existence as well as their own activities [vampires will do the same for them that they do for vampires] but its not any more believable or less than what was before.<br /> <br /> You either buy into idea that the undead and fighting them is a good chronicle premise or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where that argument it's a bit patronizing, it's where that's the way to do it.<br /> <br /> the way I see it: They needed to be wildly successful so people would take them seriously, but not so much they would destroy the setting - so they had to stop at an awkward middle point where they, on one hand are capable off:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Second Inquisition's biggest operation wasn't Vienna, which was apparently, &quot;Al-Qaeda detonates a bomb in an old castle in Austria and European Special Forces and police respond&quot; but The Fall of London where martial law was declared for a week and the result was a massive backlash by the public </div> </div> </div>W/O somehow ending hunted themselves by the authorities nor endangering the Masquerade<br /> <br /> And on the other:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Normally, a Second Inquisition operation will consist of something more akin to, &quot;A bunch of guys in an unmarked van burns down a house and if the police show up, they show badges and say that they were investigating a meth lab that apparently blew. Didn't you get the paperwork?&quot; </div> </div> </div>The SI suffered from a bad case of abusing the Worf Effect.<br /> <br /> I don't abhor it, but I don't think it's brillant writting either - and I HATE when people oscilate between them being, as you said: the same hunters but 3 times in number. But then they say - like you also said, that they &quot;does have to be influential enough to do all it does and cover up vampire existence as well as their own activities&quot;<br /> <br /> I would be happy enough if people would at least side for ONE of these (dispersed organization of cells with little organization, could be hunted by the acutal &quot;alphabet agencies&quot; vs. nigh-omnipotent influence everywhere, somehow) - after that I can accept your Doylist argument that, perhaps, the SI isn't the maximum in realism but neither it's Vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T20:34:26-08:00","id":1437318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437316#post1437316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't abhor it, but I don't think it's brillant writting either - and I HATE when people oscilate between them being, as you said: the same hunters but 3 times in number. But then they say - like you also said, that they &quot;does have to be influential enough to do all it does and cover up vampire existence as well as their own activities&quot;<br /> <br /> I would be happy enough if people would at least side for ONE of these (dispersed organization of cells with little organization, could be hunted by the acutal &quot;alphabet agencies&quot; vs. nigh-omnipotent influence everywhere, somehow) - after that I can accept your Doylist argument that, perhaps, the SI isn't the maximum in realism but neither it's Vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, FBI agents secretly under the control of the Camarilla investigating a Right Wing paramilitary conspiracy in the FBI (the SI) would be pretty damn interesting actually.<br /> <br /> I actually did something similar with the SAD vs. the NWO.<br /> <br /> The NWO would be able to easily smash the former but they actually couldn't believe the SAD wasn't under the control of mages so they let it fester longer than it should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T23:09:48-08:00","id":1437327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437318#post1437318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, FBI agents secretly under the control of the Camarilla investigating a Right Wing paramilitary conspiracy in the FBI (the SI) would be pretty damn interesting actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the same opinion, altrough that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> It could also be humans doing their job for once, too. But the latter would be better as potential risk for a story where the SI are protagonists, than for a vampire story<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The &quot;inner&quot; SI that knows the whole, and does stuff like control britanic goverment like a puppet w/o revealing the secret, it's what's more jarring to me. One has to question at what point your excellency becomes so surreal that it becomes magic with another name.<br /> <br /> But ultimately my point would be to choose where the SI stands.<br /> <br /> I can buy the badass-normal Illuminatus existing, with some effort. I can't buy them having those capabilities only when the plot demands so.<br /> <br /> What I tend to see it's that SI varies so wildly in capability depending on the current needs, that I can't know if such an idea of FBI vs. FBI it's a posibility (it isn't a real danger if the &quot;powers that be&quot; know, nor if the SI exists &quot;above&quot; the system somehow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T01:23:26-08:00","id":1437332,"title":"","content":"I've been enjoying some of the ideas thrown out in this thread, figure I'll throw a few chips in.<br /> <br /> I think it is fair to acknowledge that some of the actions taken by the Second Inquisition strain disbelief; Vienna and London are pretty huge events, and I think assuming that those actions are successful because of other, more powerful, forces acting behind the scenes is reasonable. Or at least those more powerful forces were not intervening to prevent it. But I do find it frustrating how often discussions of the SI tend to frame the matter in very 'white room' terms of Kindred vs. Second Inquisition, like each side is collectively committed to an all-out total war. The &quot;actual&quot; situation is likely to be far messier than that, on both sides.<br /> <br /> To start, if it was &quot;Total War&quot; like I discussed above, the Kindred would win. If every Methuselah united under one banner to crush the kine, that would be it. Unless you take 6+ Disciplines out of the equation, or their equivalents. That is very much not going to be the situation of the struggle against the SI, however, because that same ridiculous power that would allow Methuselahs to crush the SI makes it just as easy for them to dismiss it. For them, it is just a passing phase to be ignored, if not taken advantage of. There simply aren't enough True Faith paladins out there for the SI to win a total war against the most powerful ranks of the Kindred, and the Methuselahs will almost always find a way to endure and hide in the shadows. But that means that those Methuselahs likely aren't going to be raising their god-like powers against this new &quot;threat,&quot; especially not within the first few decades, a relatively short time for millennia-old vampires. Vienna and London are the only things that could alter that perception, but one of those has already been revealed to have been reasonably managed by an Ancient. They have bigger fish to fry, deadlier threats to concern themselves with.<br /> <br /> Yes, all of that kind of ignored the Beckoning. I am wont to do that, it's one thing from V5 I really haven't managed to warm up to even a bit, albeit from my second-hand mostly-interested-in-the-plot-points perspective.<br /> <br /> But as soon as this becomes a struggle of Elders and Ancilla versus Hunters, the playing field has been leveled significantly. The most powerful Elders may have a small handful of 6+ Disciplines, but they are no longer blood-sucking demigods that laugh at the plans of mice and men. And remember, most Kindred are not paying significant attention to what is happening beyond their particular Domain, which tends to focus around a single metropolitan area. How much do the individual Princes of cities know about the &quot;Second Inquisition,&quot; especially in the early years? How much does the average Kindred know? Factor in the fact that the Kindred are a bunch of backstabbing bloodsucking infighting monsters that can supernaturally go off the handle under bad conditions, and how quickly do you reasonably expect them to organize any kind of collective action, especially when, again, the puppet-masters among the Kindred that tend to look at the bigger picture are a) not feeling threatened, and b) potentially looking to take advantage of the situation? The SI can be an existential threat to 90% of the vampire population precisely because the 10% that could do something about it are also the least motivated to do so.<br /> <br /> To begin looking at things from the other side, the main advantage the SI has is organization and common cause. Most Kindred are not soldiers, they are not dedicated to a cause and trained to work as a unit to achieve that cause. For the most part, vampire society isn't organizing to hunt the SI, but the SI is organizing to hunt them. Again, the vast majority of Kindred society is largely entangled in local affairs, while the SI has members who are used to picking up and going where they need to. Maybe 2021 or so would be the year when the Kindred would finally say &quot;Ok, this has gone on long enough, time for some radical F-ing friendship and teamwork, folks,&quot; but I don't find it especially unbelievable that they might need a decade or two to get their shit together.<br /> <br /> Some of the discussion above has gone back and forth on whether or not a loose network of alphabet-agencies, inquisitors, and less official groups, could maintain the communication networks necessary for the actions attributed to the SI. But really, to question that is to question well-established premises of the setting that are included in the SI. The Society of Leopold is probably the best example, but groups like the Arcanum and Special Affairs Department may also qualify. Specifically, they are groups which have managed to maintain functioning communication networks throughout extended conflict with supernatural opposition, without being hopelessly compromised. Consider those groups the informational core of the SI. Not only would they be able to provide information that less-experienced participating groups may lack, but also the knowledge of how to effectively maintain communications and limit subversion. Are people going to be compromised? Of course. But again, at least some of these organizations have been accepted as operating in the World of Darkness for an extended period of time, and being able to endure. And from there, the rest is just slow, steady, and likely very painful, progress. And it's not likely that all information is being shared equally. But all it takes is enough information being share effectively, and those groups can become surprisingly threatening to the 90+% of Kindred that aren't millennia-old blood-gods.<br /> <br /> But to briefly address the original question at the start of the thread, yes and then some. No matter what, revealing the truth of the existence of the Kindred promises disruption of all sorts. While cynicism is very much at home in the World of Darkness, a more optimistic interpretation of why they avoid the disruption that would come with revealing the existence of vampires is that they hope they can end the problem without that kind of chaos ever being necessary, which makes all the more sense with the relatively solid, but by no means perfect, information that the SI has generally been depicted as having access to.<br /> <br /> P.S. I should admit, I do like to imagine at least a pro-Pogrom faction of the Technocracy as being a covert backer of the SI, at kind of the opposite end of the spectrum from the SoL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T05:39:38-08:00","id":1437343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437318#post1437318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, FBI agents secretly under the control of the Camarilla investigating a Right Wing paramilitary conspiracy in the FBI (the SI) would be pretty damn interesting actually.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing of vampires'd be a pretty left-wing thing to do, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T06:28:56-08:00","id":1437344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437315#post1437315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but making the SI the good guys isn't going to make the situation better because presumably the game is about the PCs killing and winning over their antagonists. It seems like it would compound the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if by \u201cantagonist\u201d you mean \u201cevery NPC with a 7+ Humanity who isn\u2019t of immediate use\u201d and by \u201cwinning over\u201d you mean \u201cstab in the back for personal advantage.\u201d<br /> <br /> They turned sexually abused runaway children over to be eaten by Camarilla higher ups (justified by them as the kids being Masquerade breaches and blaming the Thinbloods for that) in exchange for boons from the Prince. This after learning the ins and outs of the Thinbloods\u2019 charity efforts (ostensibly to help them), then took it over and use it to enrich themselves instead of helping runaways.<br /> <br /> The only reason their Humanity scores aren\u2019t lower is the rules won\u2019t let them lose too many at once and the hierarchy of sins makes calls for rolling less frequent the lower you go.<br /> <br /> They took one look at a setting where the powerful were elitist dicks and there were good and downtrodden people in need and, instead of the expected \u201cwe should work against the elitist dicks and help the downtrodden\u201d it was instead decided \u201cwe should cozy up to the elitist dicks and screw over the downtrodden.\u201d<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t subtle about it either. The very first things they learned is the Prince gives out \u201cone free clean-up\u201d tokens (good only for that year, no banking them, but they can be traded) every Christmas as gifts to his fellow Kindred so they can murder any human they want and Prince\u2019s men will clean up any mess (including making any investigations or witnesses disappear) with no favor owed. They also learned the Ventrue primogen (based on a real slave trader from colonial-era Boston) can only feed on slaves so he keeps a herd of trafficked prostitutes as his property. Their first Camarilla party involved humans bound and gagged as \u201crefreshments.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Thinbloods were literally giving away everything they could to protect and support abused kids and they turned them and the kids over so they could be eaten by the depraved assholes I described above.<br /> <br /> What including a good version of the Society of St. Leopold (for ease of discussion lets call this version the Paladins so its easier if we need to do side-by-sides) does is A) make me, the Storyteller, feel better about continuing the campaign. -and- B) gives the one still moral PC some non-asshole allies they can align with.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t create all these villainous NPCs to survive the campaign. My campaigns are always about good overcoming evil. If the players decide they\u2019re going to sidle up to evil then they get the consequences of their choices. I will enjoy their reactions as, one-by-one, all their villainous allies go down, the trafficked women get rescued and all their schemes for power start to come undone.<br /> <br /> The very first NPC to speak to any PC was that Franciscan friar mentor I mentioned who reminded the dhampir PC before they began to infiltrate the vampires (while all the players were listening) that \u201cthe wages of sin is death.\u201d<br /> <br /> When the Paladins show up, the PCs will be given every possible chance to turn back from their path. The Paladins are not hate-filled fanatics. God can forgive any sin if the sinner repents of it.<br /> <br /> If they still refuse, then that\u2019s their choice and I\u2019d be a bad Storyteller if I didn\u2019t let them receive the consequences of their choices. If they will not willingly stop hurting innocents for personal gain, then the consequence is that the Paladins will attempt to stop them and I have no problem administering a TPK (or near TPK) if that\u2019s what the consequences logically call for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 02-28-2021, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T07:05:11-08:00","id":1437345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437343#post1437343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing of vampires'd be a pretty left-wing thing to do, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the way you want to run it, sure. It's your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437327#post1437327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm of the same opinion, altrough that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> It could also be humans doing their job for once, too. But the latter would be better as potential risk for a story where the SI are protagonists, than for a vampire story<br /> <br /> The &quot;inner&quot; SI that knows the whole, and does stuff like control britanic goverment like a puppet w/o revealing the secret, it's what's more jarring to me. One has to question at what point your excellency becomes so surreal that it becomes magic with another name.<br /> <br /> But ultimately my point would be to choose where the SI stands.<br /> <br /> I can buy the badass-normal Illuminatus existing, with some effort. I can't buy them having those capabilities only when the plot demands so.<br /> <br /> What I tend to see it's that SI varies so wildly in capability depending on the current needs, that I can't know if such an idea of FBI vs. FBI it's a posibility (it isn't a real danger if the &quot;powers that be&quot; know, nor if the SI exists &quot;above&quot; the system somehow).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the funny thing is that I see what you're having a problem with and I think that's a feature rather than a bug. It's also something that I think is directly baked into the Second Inquisition rather than something that was unintended. I do think the Second Inquisition is simultaneously an extremely influential and powerful organization that is constantly tripping over itself. Because I think of the SI as not a single overarching conspiracy. I see it as a loose alliance of a dozen conspiracies that include very powerful ones and very weak ones in a mirror of the Camarilla itself.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> The NSA part of the Second Inquisition has billions of dollars in dark money, blackmail information on politicians, contacts with politics in the highest levels of government, advanced equipment that bleeds against the Consensus, probable Numina in psychics, and their own frigging satellites.<br /> <br /> What the NSA doesn't have is actual agents on the ground despite what Hollywood says or authority to operate their own missions. To that, they turn to the SAD and Inquisition who have plenty of people who are willing to walk the beat on the ground and set fire to things. They are well-trained in killing vampires as much as humans can be and historically have had reasonable success doing so. However, they don't have the information or money or influence to do much until now.<br /> <br /> Below them are the new recruits like the Night's Cross or Hunters the SI has freed from jail. These are basically militia nuts, mercs, and ex-soldiers the other SI people have picked up. They lack experience and a proper fear of the undead that they'll happily try to attack vampires at night or blow up a building with C4. They're probably the grunts of the SI but they have an endless supply of these guys.<br /> <br /> In addition to these guys there's also the Arcanum who don't actually do any of the hunting but have been researching for centuries and compiling lists ala the Talamasca that they've officially just handed over. They also include a shit ton of rich assholes and hedge mages who have been &quot;vampire-proofing&quot; the minds and bases of the SI.<br /> <br /> Any of these groups can be screwed with individually but as a whole appear to be stronger than they actually are. Which is to say I think the Arcanum, SAD, and NSA can cover up the leaks of vampirism pretty well between them but the soldiers on the ground are still squishy humans.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Patronage:<br /> <br /> I don't think the SI should be controlled by vampires but I do think that it should benefit from some quislings in the ranks of the supernatural or at least people who have been inclined to support it rather than undermine it. This is a way for the Jyhad to be shown in its complexity rather than undermine the idea that the SI is a revolt of the human race.<br /> <br /> In my campaign, I did this:<br /> <br /> * The success of the Fall of London is because the SI was directly being aided by the human branch of the Culr of Mithras. Ancient families who have been doing things like controlling the British Isles and the media since the dawn of time. Nowhere else would this have been possible if not for the acts of a deranged methuselah even if no one on the ground knew why the government suddenly knew about vampires and didn't seem to care after a week.<br /> <br /> (This is canon to the Fall of London, FYI).<br /> <br /> * The Harbingers did the same in Italy for the Mausoleum.<br /> <br /> (Ditto)<br /> <br /> * Whoeever made the Vienna chantry vulnerable. Not because the SI didn't strike at the heart of the Tremere but because vampires are self-defeating enough that they were willing to betray one of their strongholds to the enemy.<br /> <br /> (No idea who this is)<br /> <br /> * (Non-Canon) Marcus Vitel is doing the same in Washington D.C. in my games because the 2000 year old Lasombra has apocalypse dreams of wiping out all other vampires.<br /> <br /> * (Non-Canon) Alamut was hit by multiple bunker buster bombs by the US military due to Marcus using his knowledge of its location. It was one of the biggest victories of the SI and they don't even know it happened.<br /> <br /> * (Non-Canon): Pentex is supplying the SI with equipment as is the Traditions (Arcanum, Oof, Celestial Choir, Inquisition) and Technocracy (NWO for NSA) because it suitds their piurposes. This is like a dozen people but very rich and powerful people. Just enough to keep things going in the early days and increase their effectiveness. The Virtual Adepts were the people who actually broke into Schrek.net and gave the NSA their findings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437344#post1437344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if by \u201cantagonist\u201d you mean \u201cevery NPC with a 7+ Humanity who isn\u2019t of immediate use\u201d and by \u201cwinning over\u201d you mean \u201cstab in the back for personal advantage.\u201d<br /> <br /> They turned sexually abused runaway children over to be eaten by Camarilla higher ups (justified by them as the kids being Masquerade breaches and blaming the Thinbloods for that) in exchange for boons from the Prince. This after learning the ins and outs of the Thinbloods\u2019 charity efforts (ostensibly to help them), then took it over and use it to enrich themselves instead of helping runaways.<br /> <br /> The only reason their Humanity scores aren\u2019t lower is the rules won\u2019t let them lose too many at once and the hierarchy of sins makes calls for rolling less frequent the lower you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you might want to say its not your kind of game then. Yeesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-28-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T07:43:28-08:00","id":1437348,"title":"","content":"<b>The Second Inquisition and Supernatural Infiltration</b><br /> <br /> A couple of fun-factoids:<br /> <br /> 1. If you read Project: Twilight then you'd note the SAD *IS* hopelessly compromised or was by 2001. The irony was that it was hopelessly compromised in a way that meant it kept trudging along instead of being destroyed. Its regional directors included:<br /> <br /> * The second in command working for the New World Order (albeit she didn't realize it)<br /> * Its third in command working for Pentex (dark money) and waiting for his cushy job post-retirement.<br /> * Its Regional Directors including a goddamn Silver Fang Kinfolk who was the daughter of a previous director.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla wasn't able to get a handle on the SAD because a bunch of other supernatural factions were already there and were cancelling each other out to let the SAD basically do its own thing.<br /> <br /> This isn't the way I'd do it for the SI but it does kind of show the humor value of the fact that real life intelligence services have done the same. J. Edgar Hoover actually saved the communist party from bankruptcy in the USA by pumping in so much money to watch it.<br /> <br /> 2. I really liked the fact that the CAMARILLA book mentions that the reason the SI got off the ground with the NSA was because one specific vampire Elder (maybe a Justicar or Archon) was handling its manipulation of the organization through a woman named Felicity Price.<br /> <br /> At one point, Price's Dominate just vanished and they had about 20 years of being a vampire stooge come back to them. Presumably because said Elder was killed or Beckoned. There wasn't an Elder there to immediately take over her handling because her master wasn't going to show their holdlings to potential rivals. The secrecy of the Camarilla undercutting it.<br /> <br /> This is just one of those kind of random things that can happen in the Jyhad. The Camarilla had a lot of things under wraps but if you remove key players then the Jenga tower collapses.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T09:37:45-08:00","id":1437358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437348#post1437348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Second Inquisition and Supernatural Infiltration</b><br /> <br /> A couple of fun-factoids:<br /> <br /> 1. If you read Project: Twilight then you'd note the SAD *IS* hopelessly compromised or was by 2001. The irony was that it was hopelessly compromised in a way that meant it kept trudging along instead of being destroyed. Its regional directors included...</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I'm sure the vampires could've gotten involved there anyhow, not necessarily through hard means (A ghoul, Dominate) but with the soft stuff (promises of a lofty possition, an embrace, threatening families...) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I really liked the fact that the CAMARILLA book mentions that the reason the SI got off the ground with the NSA was because one specific vampire Elder (maybe a Justicar or Archon) was handling its manipulation of the organization through a woman named Felicity Price.<br /> <br /> At one point, Price's Dominate just vanished and they had about 20 years of being a vampire stooge come back to them. Presumably because said Elder was killed or Beckoned. There wasn't an Elder there to immediately take over her handling because her master wasn't going to show their holdlings to potential rivals. The secrecy of the Camarilla undercutting it. </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as one of dumbest plot points we have. Vampires are pretty competitive and cynical, what'd be the happenstance that it was just that guy with a finger in the NSA and nobody else had the idea to put a finger in the NSA while nobody else had the wits to watch a guy of that status? <br /> (also, Dominate doesn't become ineffective when the vampire dies? That'd make every final death of someone using forgetful mind a whole-city disaster sweep)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T09:51:32-08:00","id":1437360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437344#post1437344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn\u2019t create all these villainous NPCs to survive the campaign. My campaigns are always about good overcoming evil. If the players decide they\u2019re going to sidle up to evil then they get the consequences of their choices. I will enjoy their reactions as, one-by-one, all their villainous allies go down, the trafficked women get rescued and all their schemes for power start to come undone.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">....and I have no problem administering a TPK (or near TPK) if that\u2019s what the consequences logically call for.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> vampire's a setting where evil'll continue if you don't do anything about it. That's my &quot;moral lesson&quot;. Having good auto-win because it's good isn't exactly morally bankrupt, but I find it pretty... it's selling a lie, and that's not a good thing. <br /> <br /> Also getting plot armoured-to-death never feels like the actions of a righteous storyteller. Kill me for playing stupid, not for playing mean (to some npcs who aren't real) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Paladins show up, the PCs will be given every possible chance to turn back from their path. The Paladins are not hate-filled fanatics. God can forgive any sin if the sinner repents of it. </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the idea here, but at the same time.... unless these paladins have a method of curing vampires, 'forgiveness' should mean 'you die and don't go to hell' not 'they let you go'. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T10:08:31-08:00","id":1437363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437358#post1437358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as one of dumbest plot points we have. Vampires are pretty competitive and cynical, what'd be the happenstance that it was just that guy with a finger in the NSA and nobody else had the idea to put a finger in the NSA while nobody else had the wits to watch a guy of that status?<br /> (also, Dominate doesn't become ineffective when the vampire dies? That'd make every final death of someone using forgetful mind a whole-city disaster sweep)</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as making vampires look dumber not smarter. If they can't make a mistake then they can't succeed. If another vampire knew the other vampires' holdings and when they went off the rails then the original vampire was a shitty Elder. A true vampire's network of power is invisible and unassailable.<br /> <br /> At least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I think power vacuums are very good things to show in the game. <b>&quot;Why don't we kill the Prince?&quot;</b> should have the answer, &quot;Because then we need to have a bunch of people scramble to gain control over the media, police, and city government?&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides, we already KNOW the vampire who was in charge of the NSA and American Intelligence assets because it was stated to be <b>Marcus Vitel</b>. Theo Bell put him in the ground and then the city of Washington D.C was under the Sabbat's control before Vykos disappeared. That right there probably indicates who Felicity Price's master was and why she fell back into free will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-28-2021, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T23:09:11-08:00","id":1437429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437048#post1437048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They also don't register as &quot;blanks&quot; and depending on how people justify racism against them in the setting, it'd be interesting to see how that affects thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be that the Toreador were the &quot;Human&quot; clan, and along comes the Thin-bloods to take that distinction and do a lot of thing that the Toreador want to do but can't. I would imagine the Degenerates are pretty pissed off at the mercurians","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T23:14:57-08:00","id":1437430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437332#post1437332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been enjoying some of the ideas thrown out in this thread, figure I'll throw a few chips in.<br /> <br /> I think it is fair to acknowledge that some of the actions taken by the Second Inquisition strain disbelief; Vienna and London are pretty huge events, and I think assuming that those actions are successful because of other, more powerful, forces acting behind the scenes is reasonable. Or at least those more powerful forces were not intervening to prevent it. But I do find it frustrating how often discussions of the SI tend to frame the matter in very 'white room' terms of Kindred vs. Second Inquisition, like each side is collectively committed to an all-out total war. The &quot;actual&quot; situation is likely to be far messier than that, on both sides.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that the SI had Mages within their midst (either as a member or as a hired third party) to make the implausible possible. Get a powerful enough mage and you can do some amazing things. Then again, this is the 5th edition universe, and mages might get nerfed if and when M5 comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T23:32:07-08:00","id":1437433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437429#post1437429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It used to be that the Toreador were the &quot;Human&quot; clan, and along comes the Thin-bloods to take that distinction and do a lot of thing that the Toreador want to do but can't. I would imagine the Degenerates are pretty pissed off at the mercurians</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of the Toreador as the unsung masters of the Camarilla. I think of them behind the destruction of the Thin Bloods just because their Humanity pisses them off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T00:17:09-08:00","id":1437436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437429#post1437429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It used to be that the Toreador were the &quot;Human&quot; clan, and along comes the Thin-bloods to take that distinction and do a lot of thing that the Toreador want to do but can't. I would imagine the Degenerates are pretty pissed off at the mercurians</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah the Toreador are just talking shit. They're in-tune with human culture, but that's more for exploitation. They're probably the nastiest clan, because they're not the Ventrue fucking up the masses from the confines of his castle, or the Nosferatu who you don't notice, or the Brujah who just looks like trouble and you know to avoid him, or the malkavians who have very select victims most of the time. The Toreador are the kind of people who'll build you up, play you like a fiddle, leave you devestated, and then brag about what a good person they are. But more importantly they're the epitome of neoliberal hypocrisy; they'll say what you want to hear, they'll act like martyrs, and they'll continually act against your best interests. The Toreador are one of wealthiest clans in the setting (granted, there's more of them) and yet they'll continually pretend to be more human and down to earth while spurning the low clans for not being classy enough. Oh, and the fine art industry's just an exercise for tax evasion. <br /> <br /> I love to hate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-01-2021, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T01:03:34-08:00","id":1437439,"title":"","content":"I had my PC (A Malkavian) explain Toreadors as thus, &quot;Toreadors feel more than any other clan, which means that while most vampires can feel hatred and anger, these are the only clan that feel very human <i>spite</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> He also said, &quot;A Ventrue will kill you for not kneeling, a Nosferatu will kill you if you're arrogant or vain, a Tremere will kill you for your secrets, a Gangrel will kill you for your blood without ever thinking twice about it afterward, a Brujah will kill you because they felt like it, and God knows why a Malkavian will kill you, but a Toreador is the only Clan that will systematically destroy your life as well as your family's just because you wore the wrong shoes to their party.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-01-2021, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T03:54:48-08:00","id":1437452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437439#post1437439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He also said, &quot;A Ventrue will kill you for not kneeling, a Nosferatu will kill you if you're arrogant or vain, a Tremere will kill you for your secrets, a Gangrel will kill you for your blood without ever thinking twice about it afterward, a Brujah will kill you because they felt like it, and God knows why a Malkavian will kill you, but a Toreador is the only Clan that will systematically destroy your life as well as your family's just because you wore the wrong shoes to their party.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I want to tidy this up a bit and steal it. Permission/who to reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T05:43:34-08:00","id":1437465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437345#post1437345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the funny thing is that I see what you're having a problem with and I think that's a feature rather than a bug. It's also something that I think is directly baked into the Second Inquisition rather than something that was unintended. I do think the Second Inquisition is simultaneously an extremely influential and powerful organization that is constantly tripping over itself. Because I think of the SI as not a single overarching conspiracy. I see it as a loose alliance of a dozen conspiracies that include very powerful ones and very weak ones in a mirror of the Camarilla itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're quite seeing it yet. There's a diametral difference between &quot;an extremely influential and powerful organization that is constantly tripping over itself&quot;, that got big help from some supernatural powers (Mithras) than can abuse of &quot;a wizard did id&quot; - and being able to do any of those stunts w/o anything magic going on.<br /> <br /> Compare your position with Chris position on Viena:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the SI material released so far (mostly in the V5 Camarilla book) doesn\u2019t indicate these are isolated cells; they mention interagency (and international) cooperation and approved black ops budgets in the billions. The Tremere Chantry in Vienna was hit by a joint SOCOM (United States Special Operations Command) task force... <b>meaning approval for the strike came from at least the level of the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff if not the President of the United States.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot more ingrained in the &quot;powers that be&quot; than being an obscure alphabet agency conspiration with money but no agents on the ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally, a Second Inquisition operation will consist of something more akin to, &quot;A bunch of guys in an unmarked van burns down a house and if the police show up, they show badges and say that they were investigating a meth lab that apparently blew. Didn't you get the paperwork?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you get the paperwork? wouldn't be a rethoric question in this scenario: The paperwork does exist, so you evidently didn't got it...If Biden, and/or everyone that's someone in the Pentagon, know - then you cannot have a scenario where the SI has real problems with other authorities.<br /> <br /> Also, in order to fully explain Viena, you would want to have co-opted the powers that be in Austria to a similar extent. So they would ignore or burry the investigation, comforming with the official statement.But at that point we have the an unoficial organization of Goverments all over the world agreeing on one thing: To kill vampires.<br /> <br /> This is not the scenario you're pressenting. You're presenting a much more moderate scenario, where the SI it's an occult conspiration (that could get in trouble with the *other* alphabet agencies, if discovered), and where supernatural influence it's being used to explain quite a lot of stuff<br /> <br /> I'm ok with that choice. But it has consequences - WoD isn't a 100% realistic setting, but it's relatively gritty and down to earth compared with many other settings.<br /> <br /> For instance: Rambo it's described as a badass-normal in his own fiction, but I think a single human beating whole armies with a gun wouldn't be very realistic in WoD (I, at least, would think he's a mage - and one soon to suffer from Domino Effect)<br /> <br /> IF every authority that has real power isn't on it - you're, in my eyes, implicilty accepting supernatural influence would be needed to realistically wave away some of the most outrageous stunts at some point (like the authors did with London), least you end breaking incredulity. Either that or you're making no sense<br /> <br /> (like when you argued the SI could get away with nuking bangladesh w/o magic, and w/o being the NWO in all but name - that makes no sense. And there I can't accept your Doylist and Watsonian aguments becuse nothing in WoD it's so unrealistic nor has been so boldly shitting on common sense as that idea, ever - well, except the Sabbat making cities disappear. And that was retconned because it was too silly. So, same thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-01-2021, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T07:26:10-08:00","id":1437476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437452#post1437452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to tidy this up a bit and steal it. Permission/who to reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Have at it.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:22:02-08:00","id":1437485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437430#post1437430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It could be that the SI had Mages within their midst (either as a member or as a hired third party) to make the implausible possible. Get a powerful enough mage and you can do some amazing things. Then again, this is the 5th edition universe, and mages might get nerfed if and when M5 comes out.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As my tiny little note at the end of my post mentioned, I am very sympathetic to the idea of Mages backing the Second Inquisition, though likely more from the fringes; going back to the Society of Leopold, I could imagine them being in touch with a handful of fundamentalist Choristers, even if they don't know precisely what they are beyond &quot;holy men with divine powers.&quot; </span></span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But as people have discussed, there is the question of what you want the SI to be in your story, and if they're meant to be the embodiment of &quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah!&quot; then it undermines that more than a little bit to have *every* major accomplishment attributed to them be the result of &quot;Secret Masters&quot; (whether those be Mages, other Vampires, whatever). </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:34:11-08:00","id":1437487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437465#post1437465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you're quite seeing it yet. There's a diametral difference between &quot;an extremely influential and powerful organization that is constantly tripping over itself&quot;, that got big help from some supernatural powers (Mithras) than can abuse of &quot;a wizard did id&quot; - and being able to do any of those stunts w/o anything magic going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're getting at but I think that's not necessarily completely irreconcilable. What I've been getting at is I think the Second Inquisition appears larger and more influential than it is because it is a mole that is buried deep inside the larger Intelligence Apparatus. Also, its biggest accomplishments are things that they can't easily replicate.<br /> <br /> While I may be excusing bad writing by having the United States launch a Presidentially-authorized attack on the Tremere chantry in an ally's sovereign territory, the thing is that the President doesn't need to know about vampires to do so. The Second Inquisition doesn't need to have access to the President and his cabinet, just the people providing information to him. It'd require a lot of influence and planning but the SI explicitly does have people in the NSA and that means they can alter SIGNIT as one of their genuine abilities.<br /> <br /> I mentioned earlier that in my home game, Alamut of the Banu Haqim is a smoking crater and Ur-Shulgi is once more back in torpor (or finally dead). This was not due to the Second Inquisition having their own access to bunker buster bombs. No, it was the perfect storm of coincidences and gentle nudges that Alamut was located in Syria and they could manipulate the mainstream US military to attack a position that was nominally invulnerable to attack. Why? Because bombing a seemingly abandoned mountain was not something they needed to justify once they mentioned it was &quot;full of insurgents.&quot;<br /> <br /> I had a similar read on the Technocratic Union that its seeming omnipresence and power was less because it was actually the ruler of the world but because they could muster the influence of other groups. The Technocracy using tactics like Agent Smith in the Matrix where the only thing the police know about Morpheus is that he's a &quot;terrorist&quot; and &quot;the most dangerous man in the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't think the Second Inquisition can pull off what they did in Vienna, Austria again. Manufacturing the idea that an &quot;abandoned&quot; castle or minor historical landmark was full of terrorists with chemical weapons is a very different thing than, say, pulling off an attack on all the vampires in a city and even that probably burned a massive amount of the SI's credibility/resources.<br /> <br /> I admit this is my interpretation of the SI and I may have put more thought into it than some fans or STs think it deserves. I think it's how I would play it and not a bad interpretation of the data we've been presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437485#post1437485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As my tiny little note at the end of my post mentioned, I am very sympathetic to the idea of Mages backing the Second Inquisition, though likely more from the fringes; going back to the Society of Leopold, I could imagine them being in touch with a handful of fundamentalist Choristers, even if they don't know precisely what they are beyond &quot;holy men with divine powers.&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But as people have discussed, there is the question of what you want the SI to be in your story, and if they're meant to be the embodiment of &quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah!&quot; then it undermines that more than a little bit to have *every* major accomplishment attributed to them be the result of &quot;Secret Masters&quot; (whether those be Mages, other Vampires, whatever). </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A friend of mine said if you're going to make the SI controlled by supernaturals, then why not just make it the Technocracy vs. Vampires as started by Operation: Ragnarok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:47:22-08:00","id":1437488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437487#post1437487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine said if you're going to make the SI controlled by supernaturals, then why not just make it the Technocracy vs. Vampires as started by Operation: Ragnarok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, so yes, basically. Lol.<br /> <br /> I'll probably come back and flesh this out a bit more, but I need to run out the door for a while. But I like finding somewhere in the middle, rather than a strict binary of &quot;the SI is completely independent from other supernatural factions&quot; versus &quot;the SI only continues to function because it's a catspaw of Mages, Vampires, etc.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:37:58-08:00","id":1437513,"title":"","content":"Could be that the Technocracy needs a proxy because they know they'd lose against vamps (and their other enemies) in a protracted conflict; mages may win battles, but vampires win wars. Vamps have more numbers, easier replenishment, and more mortal influence. As much as I'd love a game of blasting vampires with laser rifles and hiding behind HIT marks, it's not a likely game, and I'm all about that -believable setting- Getting these little hunter groups together seems like something they could do without getting slain. Mortals could get the CIA and the FBI and the FSB and MI6 and the People's army of spies or whatever to hunt vampires, but they can't really get the -fraction of the CIA- to get together with the -fraction of the FBI- and -Fraction of NSA- and so on to work together, because paranoia rules the day. But a mage could probably bullshit a ritual for that. One questionable thing about the technocracy getting involved is the religious groups getting involved. Sure, the SoL is by far the absolute favourite for hunting vampires, but they're mystical catholics, and while christianity's probs the -least bad- religion in the technocracy's eyes, this whacky branch of catholics really should push the buttons. <br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking about it a bit more, perhaps if the SoL infiltrated the major intelligence agencies to launch the second inquisition, I'd dig that. Trained priests acting as goverment spies? Yes please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:39:02-08:00","id":1437514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437488#post1437488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, so yes, basically. Lol.<br /> <br /> I'll probably come back and flesh this out a bit more, but I need to run out the door for a while. But I like finding somewhere in the middle, rather than a strict binary of &quot;the SI is completely independent from other supernatural factions&quot; versus &quot;the SI only continues to function because it's a catspaw of Mages, Vampires, etc.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not actually a bad idea as an alternative to the SI.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla doesn't necessarily need to know the Technocracy could exist and could be on the backfoot by just believing the Union's forces are the government.<br /> <br /> After all, how would they be able to tell the difference between Men in Black and their cloned soldiers from &quot;real&quot; government officials?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437513#post1437513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be that the Technocracy needs a proxy because they know they'd lose against vamps (and their other enemies) in a protracted conflict; mages may win battles, but vampires win wars. Vamps have more numbers, easier replenishment, and more mortal influence. As much as I'd love a game of blasting vampires with laser rifles and hiding behind HIT marks, it's not a likely game, and I'm all about that -believable setting- Getting these little hunter groups together seems like something they could do without getting slain. Mortals could get the CIA and the FBI and the FSB and MI6 and the People's army of spies or whatever to hunt vampires, but they can't really get the -fraction of the CIA- to get together with the -fraction of the FBI- and -Fraction of NSA- and so on to work together, because paranoia rules the day. But a mage could probably bullshit a ritual for that. One questionable thing about the technocracy getting involved is the religious groups getting involved. Sure, the SoL is by far the absolute favourite for hunting vampires, but they're mystical catholics, and while christianity's probs the -least bad- religion in the technocracy's eyes, this whacky branch of catholics really should push the buttons.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it a bit more, perhaps if the SoL infiltrated the major intelligence agencies to launch the second inquisition, I'd dig that. Trained priests acting as goverment spies? Yes please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that actually.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference in any hypothetical war between the Union and vampires.<br /> <br /> 1. <i><b>Vampires do not know the Union exists</b></i>. The Tremere might but as far as the undead know, mages are all Sorcerers and the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> 2. The Union could send wave after wave of cloned soldiers with false memories, HIT Marks, and their armies of partially brainwashed recruits at the undead while never wasting one of their actual mages.<br /> <br /> The big advantage the Union has is they do have their own private armies and proxy groups like Pentex. They can also make more and indeed have an entire Convention devoted to doing just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-01-2021, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T13:09:20-08:00","id":1437525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437513#post1437513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be that the Technocracy needs a proxy because they know they'd lose against vamps (and their other enemies) in a protracted conflict; mages may win battles, but vampires win wars. Vamps have more numbers, easier replenishment, and more mortal influence. As much as I'd love a game of blasting vampires with laser rifles and hiding behind HIT marks, it's not a likely game, and I'm all about that -believable setting- Getting these little hunter groups together seems like something they could do without getting slain. Mortals could get the CIA and the FBI and the FSB and MI6 and the People's army of spies or whatever to hunt vampires, but they can't really get the -fraction of the CIA- to get together with the -fraction of the FBI- and -Fraction of NSA- and so on to work together, because paranoia rules the day. But a mage could probably bullshit a ritual for that. One questionable thing about the technocracy getting involved is the religious groups getting involved. Sure, the SoL is by far the absolute favourite for hunting vampires, but they're mystical catholics, and while christianity's probs the -least bad- religion in the technocracy's eyes, this whacky branch of catholics really should push the buttons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking about it a bit more, perhaps if the SoL infiltrated the major intelligence agencies to launch the second inquisition, I'd dig that. Trained priests acting as goverment spies? Yes please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on how you define &quot;win&quot; or &quot;lose.&quot; I'm not inclined to make absolute statements about whether Gameline 1 Faction A would win an all-out conflict against Gameline 2 Faction X. Too much depends on the particular tactical and strategic decisions taken, the metaphorical or literal &quot;roll of the dice,&quot; and particular decisions about the nature of the setting that essentially amount to Storyteller fiat depending on the table you're at. I would be very confident saying that trying to get into an open shooting war with Vampires would very likely sabotage the agenda of the Technocracy, because the Masquerade would not survive it. In that sense, they would definitely lose.<br /> <br /> But Technocrats providing alphabet agencies with &quot;experimental new technology&quot; or intelligence would provide a significant advantage to the hunters with relatively little risk to the Union. It also makes sense if you see interest in actively pursuing the Pogrom against creatures like vampires as something that interests only a portion of the entire Technocracy. The Technocracy is probably as close to a monolith as you find in the WoD, but it isn't one.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Society of Leopold and religious side of the Second Inquisition is another reason I don't see all-out commitment from the Technocrats as likely. If it was their game entirely, they probably wouldn't be working too closely with religious fundamentalists. I'm not even sure if/where True Faith fits on the &quot;Reality Deviance&quot; chart, but I'm pretty sure they have some other stuff going on that the Union would wag its finger at very firmly. I tend to see the Second Inquisition as a whole in several categories. There are the alphabet agencies, there are the Inquisitors, and there are the regular hunters that are just getting better equipped and organized now that they have more quasi-legitimate backing from the first two groups. Then you have groups like the Arcanum that aren't heavily committed on the front lines, but are providing backing in the form of intelligence, equipment, etc. I imagine most Technocrat involvement as that, but more. All of these different groups are communicating more, are cooperating more, but they don't share everything, they don't really trust each other, just enough to become a much bigger problem for vampires that generally don't trust anyone if they know what's good for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437514#post1437514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not actually a bad idea as an alternative to the SI.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla doesn't necessarily need to know the Technocracy could exist and could be on the backfoot by just believing the Union's forces are the government.<br /> <br /> After all, how would they be able to tell the difference between Men in Black and their cloned soldiers from &quot;real&quot; government officials?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it as an &quot;alternative&quot; to the Second Inquistion, but rather the logical extension into the &quot;Big&quot; World of Darkness. For the thousandth time, I am a die-hard crossover fan, but I definitely do understand having to make each gameline self-contained enough that you aren't forced to buy three series just to play the one game about vampires you want to run with your friends. If the Second Inquisition was going to be included in the core V5 metaplot, it had to be something that could be explained exclusively in terms of Vampire metaplot, not Vampire + Mage, etc.<br /> <br /> But if, like me, you are a fan of the ridiculous 90s comic-book edgelord cheese that was the Week of Nightmares/Operation: Ragnarok, and the &quot;Big&quot; World of Darkness that has Kindred, Garou, Awakened, Wraiths, Changelings, and the kitchen sink, then the idea that something as big as the Second Inquisition could be happening while the entire Technocratic Union justs sits on the sideline with its thumb up its butt strains credulity more than anything. Especially since IIRC the beginnings of the Second Inquisition at least roughly line up with when Mage metaplot has the Technocracy at least temporarily thinking that they have &quot;won&quot; the Ascension War, a time where at least some of the Union might have felt they had the time and resources to focus on a different &quot;problem,&quot; one that was maybe much bigger on their radar than it had been before they had to nuke Bangladesh trying to put one down. <br /> <br /> I definitely agree that the Camarilla probably doesn't know the Technocracy, but I feel that's at least partially true in reverse as well; if anyone in the Union knows the particulars of Kindred society, it's probably a combination of a) specialists who research vampires for a living that file reports that 98% of the Union never reads or hears about, or b) individual Technocrats that have had personal encounters, relations, etc., with Kindred and have learned through experience. The Technocracy is better equipped to acquire and distribute that intelligence throughout their ranks, but it doesn't seem likely that they already have it prepared given how little attention they've mostly paid to vampires up until now. But useful intelligence and a general understanding of the &quot;situation&quot; is going to spread through the Union far more quickly than it will the society of the paranoid backstabbing Kindred, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T13:22:42-08:00","id":1437526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437525#post1437525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if, like me, you are a fan of the ridiculous 90s comic-book edgelord cheese that was the Week of Nightmares/Operation: Ragnarok, and the &quot;Big&quot; World of Darkness that has Kindred, Garou, Awakened, Wraiths, Changelings, and the kitchen sink, then the idea that something as big as the Second Inquisition could be happening while the entire Technocratic Union justs sits on the sideline with its thumb up its butt strains credulity more than anything. Especially since IIRC the beginnings of the Second Inquisition at least roughly line up with when Mage metaplot has the Technocracy at least temporarily thinking that they have &quot;won&quot; the Ascension War, a time where at least some of the Union might have felt they had the time and resources to focus on a different &quot;problem,&quot; one that was maybe much bigger on their radar than it had been before they had to nuke Bangladesh trying to put one down.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that the Camarilla probably doesn't know the Technocracy, but I feel that's at least partially true in reverse as well; if anyone in the Union knows the particulars of Kindred society, it's probably a combination of a) specialists who research vampires for a living that file reports that 98% of the Union never reads or hears about, or b) individual Technocrats that have had personal encounters, relations, etc., with Kindred and have learned through experience. The Technocracy is better equipped to acquire and distribute that intelligence throughout their ranks, but it doesn't seem likely that they already have it prepared given how little attention they've mostly paid to vampires up until now. But useful intelligence and a general understanding of the &quot;situation&quot; is going to spread through the Union far more quickly than it will the society of the paranoid backstabbing Kindred, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, it's an interesting thing to do it with the Gonzo 100% powerful 2nd Edition Technocracy but Revised had some interesting ideas too.<br /> <br /> <b>How to do it with a Broken Technocracy</b><br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of crossovers myself but I admit that any use of the Technocracy in my present games are post-Avatar Storm and that they not only have never recovered but they <i>will never recover</i>. The Technocracy used to have access to vast numbers of clones, private armies of HIT marks, and endless numbers of loyal soldiers. All of that was destroyed by the Avatar Storm and the vast majority of its members were killed with the only mid-tier boots on the ground left to pick up the pieces.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting case to pick up the pieces as its a harsher but still canonical interpretation that the Union is a shadow of its former self. Authoritarianism is back on the rise and militancy but science denial as well as global environmental collapse among other issues are everywhere. They've failed as the Secret Masters of the Earth and now Pentex, the Nephandi, or simply corrupt humans are on the rise.<br /> <br /> So in my games, I emphasize that a lot of people the Technocracy used to hold the leash of or back like the SAD or NSA's subgroups have gone on their own. The minions have since gone on to become the masters themselves. I have individuals and Technocracy remnants helping the SI but they're more interested in rebuilding the organization than waging the Ascension War, especially since the detente with the Traditions is still holding.<br /> <br /> It actually does mean that the Union fighting the Camarilla with its proxies is much more believably balanced and doesn't occupy all the resources of either group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-01-2021, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T13:40:50-08:00","id":1437529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437526#post1437526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously, it's an interesting thing to do it with the Gonzo 100% powerful 2nd Edition Technocracy but Revised had some interesting ideas too.<br /> <br /> <b>How to do it with a Broken Technocracy</b><br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of crossovers myself but I admit that any use of the Technocracy in my present games are post-Avatar Storm and that they not only have never recovered but they <i>will never recover</i>. The Technocracy used to have access to vast numbers of clones, private armies of HIT marks, and endless numbers of loyal soldiers. All of that was destroyed by the Avatar Storm and the vast majority of its members were killed with the only mid-tier boots on the ground left to pick up the pieces.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting case to pick up the pieces as its a harsher but still canonical interpretation that the Union is a shadow of its former self. Authoritarianism is back on the rise and militancy but science denial as well as global environmental collapse among other issues are everywhere. They've failed as the Secret Masters of the Earth and now Pentex, the Nephandi, or simply corrupt humans are on the rise.<br /> <br /> So in my games, I emphasize that a lot of people the Technocracy used to hold the leash of or back like the SAD or NSA's subgroups have gone on their own. The minions have since gone on to become the masters themselves. I have individuals and Technocracy remnants helping the SI but they're more interested in rebuilding the organization than waging the Ascension War, especially since the detente with the Traditions is still holding.<br /> <br /> It actually does mean that the Union fighting the Camarilla with its proxies is much more believably balanced and doesn't occupy all the resources of either group.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point about the strength of the Technocracy between editions/pre- or post-Avatar Storm is an excellent example of what I meant above about specific details likely pertaining to Storyteller fiat being a huge deal in determining &quot;who wins, X or Y?&quot; I've read a fair number of the white room debates about X vs Y, but the discussions of the enormous fleets of Cthulu-fighting warp-ships (&quot;Qui La Machines&quot;?) under Technocracy control probably did bring me the closest I've ever come to saying &quot;Nah, those guys would be the winners, hands down.&quot; But how many of those ships did survive the Avatar Storm? What resources do they have left for replenishing their fleet? Etcetera, etcetera. And again, the question of precisely what portion of the Technocracy is committed to this, some are depicted as having relatively cozy relations with some Kindred. &lt;insert joke about Syndicate also being blood-suckers&gt; A Broken Technocracy is one response, but a Technocracy that just can't agree as a whole that this is their biggest priority right now still works pretty well for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T23:43:02-08:00","id":1437581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437488#post1437488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, so yes, basically. Lol.<br /> <br /> I'll probably come back and flesh this out a bit more, but I need to run out the door for a while. But I like finding somewhere in the middle, rather than a strict binary of &quot;the SI is completely independent from other supernatural factions&quot; versus &quot;the SI only continues to function because it's a catspaw of Mages, Vampires, etc.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy only concernes themselves with Vampires that fuck with the consensus, and as such they have reached a sort of understanding with the Camarilla (and maybe the anarchs). Vampires may be reality deviants but there's bigger fish to fry. Then again, if the Union really has been infultrated by Nephandi, then all bets are off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T23:52:06-08:00","id":1437582,"title":"","content":"Something to note: as of this post the SI has been active during he reign of 4 presidents, George W. Bush, Barrack Obama, Donald J. Trump, and now Joe Biden, with the Prelude to the SI happening under Bill Clinton. I'm curious as to how the administration of each president affected the SI if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T00:06:56-08:00","id":1437585,"title":"","content":"President probably doesn't know what the hell's going on. The military budget doesn't shift between red and blue, they both like spending money there, though one side might put on airs to please their supporters, they don't care how the money is spent, so long as it's spent and they get their generous 'donations'. It'd probably trouble the president to inform them about vampires, best not do it. <br /> I doubt the heads of the alphabet agencies know what's going on. It's all a mid/low-ranking effort to hunt vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T00:58:02-08:00","id":1437588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437581#post1437581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy only concernes themselves with Vampires that fuck with the consensus, and as such they have reached a sort of understanding with the Camarilla (and maybe the anarchs). Vampires may be reality deviants but there's bigger fish to fry. Then again, if the Union really has been infultrated by Nephandi, then all bets are off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it depends on how you choose to run your game.<br /> <br /> The Union could change its opinion post-Operation: Ragnarok or Avatar Storm. Vampires were always on the extermination list. It's just the Union assumed they'd be done with the Traditions by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T01:46:26-08:00","id":1437600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437588#post1437588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it depends on how you choose to run your game.<br /> <br /> The Union could change its opinion post-Operation: Ragnarok or Avatar Storm. Vampires were always on the extermination list. It's just the Union assumed they'd be done with the Traditions by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or on the opposite end of the spectrum, the union could integrate vampires into the consensus. In the Penny Dreadful novels, the titular mage uses the paradox effect of a magic rote to create infinite cruelty free blood for her vampire employer. Also the Union is on the top of the totem pole with infinite resources so if anyone can create TruBlood it's them. There are advantages to bringing vampires out of the open. They become living citizen that have to pay taxes like the rest of us, and their skill-sets could aid in varies industries (Construction, Military, Sex, Sports, Movies etc) and their blood could become a regulated product like pot, used medicinally or recreationally. If anyone can pull it of it's the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> However I recognize significant problems with a Vampire-Human society.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The only other time Humans and vampires supposedly lived in harmony was in Carthage, and that involved blatant infernalism and degeneracy until it was sacked by Rome/The Ventrue</li> <li>Vampires are cursed by God, and as such, Christians, Muslims and Jews will oppose vampire walking among humans. Vampires converting to these religions may not be enough to inspire lynch mobs</li> <li>The SI will also oppose the transition as they see vampires as potential terrorist and as we discussed, have prevented humans from learning the truth thus far for reasons that we have also discused</li> <li>It takes two to tangle, and the Camarilla will oppose coming &quot;out of the coffin&quot;, either because this violates their precious traditions, or because they refuse to be put on equal footing with the cattle</li> <li>Vampire prefer to drink blood straight from the tap, so to speak, and some might refuse to consume synthetic blood unless it tastes really good, or it comes in some David Cronenberg style Flesh bag, or if it's infused with alcohol or Cannabis.</li> <li>Humans would object to Vampires killing violating the law whenever they declare praxis over a city or kill someone in the name of the third tradition</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T01:49:24-08:00","id":1437601,"title":"","content":"Bah, vampires and humans already live in harmony.<br /> <br /> Vampires breed us, feed us, and feed on us.<br /> <br /> What do you call a vampire ranch?<br /> <br /> A city.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T10:13:14-08:00","id":1437648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AscentionTheMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437600#post1437600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or on the opposite end of the spectrum, the union could integrate vampires into the consensus. In the Penny Dreadful novels, the titular mage uses the paradox effect of a magic rote to create infinite cruelty free blood for her vampire employer. Also the Union is on the top of the totem pole with infinite resources so if anyone can create TruBlood it's them. There are advantages to bringing vampires out of the open. They become living citizen that have to pay taxes like the rest of us, and their skill-sets could aid in varies industries (Construction, Military, Sex, Sports, Movies etc) and their blood could become a regulated product like pot, used medicinally or recreationally. If anyone can pull it of it's the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> However I recognize significant problems with a Vampire-Human society.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The only other time Humans and vampires supposedly lived in harmony was in Carthage, and that involved blatant infernalism and degeneracy until it was sacked by Rome/The Ventrue</li> <li>Vampires are cursed by God, and as such, Christians, Muslims and Jews will oppose vampire walking among humans. Vampires converting to these religions may not be enough to inspire lynch mobs</li> <li>The SI will also oppose the transition as they see vampires as potential terrorist and as we discussed, have prevented humans from learning the truth thus far for reasons that we have also discused</li> <li>It takes two to tangle, and the Camarilla will oppose coming &quot;out of the coffin&quot;, either because this violates their precious traditions, or because they refuse to be put on equal footing with the cattle</li> <li>Vampire prefer to drink blood straight from the tap, so to speak, and some might refuse to consume synthetic blood unless it tastes really good, or it comes in some David Cronenberg style Flesh bag, or if it's infused with alcohol or Cannabis.</li> <li>Humans would object to Vampires killing violating the law whenever they declare praxis over a city or kill someone in the name of the third tradition</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they *could*, but the question is, why?<br /> <br /> I feel like the extent to which True Magic can be used to overcome or ameliorate the effects of the Kindred condition tends to be one of those &quot;Storyteller fiat&quot; areas. Creating blood that can actually sustain a Kindred is likely to be a relatively heavy investment in Quintessence. Regarding the potential advantages that Kindred can bring to the table, the Union probably has a grocery list of hypertech that they're trying to push into the Consensus which can provide the same benefits without having people turn into nigh-immortal nocturnal apex predators with super powers. The Technocracy might have good reason to ignore vampires that don't make an arse of themselves for the time being, but that's not the same as having an active incentive to try and incorporate them into the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T06:06:32-08:00","id":1437946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437241#post1437241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some bigots can be really nice or selfless people, so long as you're not an object of their bigotry... but that's a muddy subject I don't tend to get into. Wanting to rid the world of vampires, at least, is a noble goal, and sometimes sacrifices should be made for noble goals; that doesn't mean you should wipe three generations because the mother was a ghoul. The level of malice you've described is just plain counterproductive. Too-stupid-to-exist organizations just shouldn't exist, outside of farcical comedy. WoD is satirical, but it's much more low-key than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say, existing in a world in which the UN child sex trafficking ring in Bosnia and Herzegovina, Rwandan genocide, Unit 731, Holocaust, and Spanish Inquisition happened. And shit like it <i>still</i> happens, one needn't look further than the Yemen conflict, Palestinian diaspora, and Chinese treatment of Uighurs for proof of that. The history of humanity is a laundry list of the worst atrocities imaginable -- many of which are <i>lionized</i> today. The citizens and government of the US to some extent still celebrate the genocide of the Native Americans, and treat it lightly otherwise.<br /> <br /> What you miss, is people involved in this shit don't wake up every morning with a comic book villain laugh, rubbing their hands together, and planning their day full of mass murder, rape, and human medical experimentation. And they don't go to bed with a Disney villain song and dance about how evilly evil they are.<br /> <br /> No, they believe they're right, and what they do is morally justified. Either in the name of making necessary sacrifices for progress, to solve for some utilitarian equation, to rid of the world of perceived evils, or simply to get rid of one group of people or another who &quot;don't have the right to exist&quot;. They do the shit they do, believing the ends justify the means, and the ends are <i>so</i> utopian, moral, or otherwise desirable that <i>any</i> means to achieve them are necessary and proper.<br /> <br /> As a hypothetical, let's say you're some poor unfortunate Vietnam draftee. You have no idea why you're fucking there; you're told you're out to stop Communists or what the fuck ever, but the reality on the ground is this is such a malaria- and dysentery-infested shithole so far removed from the developed world nobody in the world except the Vietnamese ought to give a fuck about how the Vietnamese are governed. You spend months there getting drip-fed a slow feed of propaganda the Vietnamese aren't really people, they can't govern themselves, and they need American stewardship to develop. But worse, you hear stories about the horrific shit PAVN and the VC do to American soldiers in the field or in POW camps, and how the VC mix in with the local populations, and anyone in the country at any given time can be VC.<br /> <br /> And you've seen the consequences as your buddies get sick, hurt and shipped out, and die off one by one to the local diseases, booby traps, mines, grenades, and ambushes of an enemy you're never given clear orders to fight in pitched battles or to secure and hold strategically-important ground. No, you're just shipped out on an endless Groundhog Day-esque cycle of patrols and S&amp;D missions while the casualties, rancor, and rage at your overall circumstances pile up. All the time, your buddies' horror stories and that US propaganda eat away at your brain the same way the local parasites are eating away at your gut. And the one time there's an actual battle and you actually do what you were trained to do before shipping out, it was the <i>one fucking day</i> your superiors told you nothing was going to happen and you didn't have to worry for once, and you got your collective asses handed to you by people you were told never stood a chance against you in a straight fight.<br /> <br /> Then, you set foot in My Lai and you're told if it moves, it's a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T06:23:57-08:00","id":1437949,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's not get too deep into real world tragedies if we can. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-05-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T22:52:30-08:00","id":1438077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1435985-on-the-subject-of-the-second-inquisition-the-masqurade?p=1437946#post1437946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The citizens and government of the US to some extent still celebrate the genocide of the Native Americans, and treat it lightly otherwise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some intresting thing to add in regards to these paragraph. The killing of first nation people by colonists was unintentional, at least for the most part. When the colonists arived, they inintentionally brought bacteria and diseades that the natives did not have imunity for, therefore, most of them died of disease. If their predicesors would have bred with the vikings instead of killing them on sight, they would have gained imunity needed for their Civilization to survive. We also have to keep in mind that the conflict beetween Natives and non-natives was more nuanced than it is portrayed today. First nations people were and are human, which means that they are fallible and they are capable of the cruelty, savegry and degenaracy as seen in european society. Natives waged war on other natives before the colonists came, and when the colonists came, they came, they waged war on them. In other words, the fist nation people of yesteryear were not universally nobal savages, some of them (one tribe in particular) were canibal, and some of them did not live in harmony with nature, killing buffallo en mass. This is not to say that colonists were innocent, Wounded Knee was unjustifiable, and they did force any natives they integrated to convert into Christianity or else, but all in all, the wild west situation, as I previously said, was more nuanced than &quot;Whitey bad, Native Good&quot;. Forgive me for going off topic, but I had to set the record straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage"